{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation","id":42524,"title":"[Recruitment][Exalted 2.5] Forging a Nation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-04T16:01:48-08:00","id":42524,"title":"[Recruitment][Exalted 2.5] Forging a Nation","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Recruitment for this Game is Closed</span></b></span><br /> <br /> I'm looking for a players for an PbP Exalted game, here at Onyx Path. Right now, I'm planning on it being a nation-building game out in the Hundred kingdoms, but that is currently negotiable, if anyone has a strong desire to have a different theme and/or location. As of this moment, I am leaving Solars, Lunars, Sidereals and Dragon-bloods as options for PCs.<br /> <br /> Let me know if you're interested!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 05-16-2014, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T16:11:12-08:00","id":42531,"title":"","content":"I hunger for Exalted always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T16:52:11-08:00","id":42562,"title":"","content":"I'm interested.<br /> May I please ask what house rules you are implementing, if any? Not because I won't play if some aren't used, but it makes it easeir to decide on character concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T16:56:38-08:00","id":42563,"title":"","content":"I'm down. I'd like to run a Changing Moon Lunar. Are we allowed Schaefer Lunar rules or normal chargen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T18:48:05-08:00","id":42622,"title":"","content":"I'm not into play-by-posts, but one of my favorite people ever is showing interest, so I think I'd be willing to learn if you'd be willing to teach a newbie how to play this way. I've several ideas I've wanted to run for years, including a Zenith mafia don (best for a game confined to a single city), a Full Moon gunslinger on the run trying to protect his son from those who would kill the boy for having the bad taste to have a [demon/fae/ghost] for a mother, a Chosen of Journeys who considers it his personal duty to fix all of Creation's geomancy and will work with anyone he thinks can help him save Creation; but those are just notes to myself so I won't forget them later. I'm not sure any of them would be better than an idea I might have after hearing a more detailed pitch for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T19:58:26-08:00","id":42651,"title":"","content":"Color me interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/922-hailey-mcauliffe","name":"Hailey McAuliffe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T21:46:01-08:00","id":42692,"title":"","content":"I am interested in playing either a sidereal or a solar crafter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T22:07:32-08:00","id":42698,"title":"","content":"Wow. I didn't expect such an rapid and enthusiastic reception. Welcome, all! Six players sounds like a very nice number, so i'm going to close recruitment, unless someone above chooses to bow out.<br /> <br /> @FallenEco- the only house rule that I've used in the past is the Schaefer Lunar chargen. If anyone WANTS to use a specific house rule, let me know, and I'll give it a look over.<br /> <br /> @Dietaku- yes, just put them up here so anyone else who wants to play a Lunar can have them handy too.<br /> <br /> @Jim- those ideas are all pretty cool, and all sound like they could be applicable.<br /> <br /> Since you all appear to be looking for more information before committing or starting a character, allow me to explain. Whenever I've ST'd a game in the past, I just gave a vague concept (in this case, nation-building) and a location in the setting (hundred kingdoms), and then built the story around the PCs. My intention was to do that, but if you would rather I give you a more detailed background:<br /> <br /> The nation of Novalesk lies along the Rock River north of Nasaru Redoubt. Caught in civil unrest due to a clouded succession, a ravaging horde of Wyld mutants lead by a troupe of Raksha have just invaded from the Northeast, and deathnights stalk the forests in the west.. Drawn to the chaos in the region, the Circle of young Exalts must save the nation from the hordes of chaos and death without alerting the legions of the Realm (in Greyfalls) and Lookshy to the south.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T01:16:28-08:00","id":42761,"title":"","content":"Wow, there is a lot more Lunar concepts bouncing around than I thought. In all fairness then, I won't take one. Maybe a diplomatic Lawgiver then, probably an Eclipse design to their stated job. It'll eat a lot of Favoureds but why not. I always wanted to do 1. Will have a more detailed version done soon.<br /> <br /> For Dietaku and other Lunar Fans:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b>Peter Schaefer on Lunar Character Generation</b><br /> <br /> During a private messaging session with a fan, <a href=\"http://wiki.white-wolf.com/exalted/index.php?title=Peter_Schaefer\" target=\"_blank\">Peter Schaefer</a> discussed his original intentions for <a href=\"http://wiki.white-wolf.com/exalted/index.php?title=Lunar_Exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Lunar Exalted</a> character generation:<br /> <i>Off the top of my head: </i><ul><li><i>28 Ability dots </i></li> <li><i>9/7/5 Attributes </i></li> <li><i>7 Charms (4 Caste/Favored) </i></li> <li><i>3 Knacks </i></li> <li><i>Two Favored Attributes from the three related to your Caste, two more chosen from any of the remaining seven. </i></li> </ul><br /> <i>That probably covers the important differences. Backgrounds do not cost any more for Lunars than they do for Solars; e.g., a Lunar can take up to 5 Influence without spending twice normal bonus points. Knacks cost 8xp per instead of 11xp. Nothing else comes to mind. </i><br /> These quotes were posted on <a href=\"http://www.thefreedomstone.com/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?f=6&amp;t=4381\" target=\"_blank\">The Freedom Stone Forum</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I saved the wiki page before it died. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":".  formatting 01-05-2014, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:02:12-08:00","id":42881,"title":"","content":"I am probably going to play a Sidereal of some stripe, though kingdom-building probably means I have to stray from my usual combat-focused ways... I'll have to think about it. <br /> <br /> Any other houserules we should know about? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not into play-by-posts, but one of my favorite people ever is showing interest, so I think I'd be willing to learn if you'd be willing to teach a newbie how to play this way. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure I could write essays on the different modes of playing RPGs... But don't worry, PbP doesn't bite and isn't that complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:29:47-08:00","id":42894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=42698#post42698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Jim- those ideas are all pretty cool, and all sound like they could be applicable.<br /> <br /> Since you all appear to be looking for more information before committing or starting a character, allow me to explain. Whenever I've ST'd a game in the past, I just gave a vague concept (in this case, nation-building) and a location in the setting (hundred kingdoms), and then built the story around the PCs. My intention was to do that, but if you would rather I give you a more detailed background:<br /> <br /> The nation of Novalesk lies along the Rock River north of Nasaru Redoubt. Caught in civil unrest due to a clouded succession, a ravaging horde of Wyld mutants lead by a troupe of Raksha have just invaded from the Northeast, and deathknights stalk the forests in the west.. Drawn to the chaos in the region, the Circle of young Exalts must save the nation from the hordes of chaos and death without alerting the legions of the Realm (in Greyfalls) and Lookshy to the south.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm one of those guys who can (and frequently does) come up with character concepts in a vacuum, but I always feel kind of bad about it when it's time to apply those concepts to a game, because the GM has his own world and the ideas I come up with usually have theirs too, so there's occasionally some conflict going on. I shall elucidate on my character concepts in a bit after I have a word with Omicron.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=42881#post42881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure I could write essays on the different modes of playing RPGs... But don't worry, PbP doesn't bite and isn't that complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mostly worried about etiquette. I am a live gamer mostly, where timing counts for a lot; I can read the people around me, choose my words so I don't bore people with how much time I'm taking, and expect a rapid reply from whoever's sitting across the table. I've never done a game like this before, where I don't have those abilities. I just don't want to step on anyone's toes, is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:25:34-08:00","id":42973,"title":"","content":"Ah, thanks, FallenEco. I, unfortunately, didn't save the wiki page, and was having problems finding it elsewhere. <br /> <br /> Omnicron- No other house rules, unless someone can convince me that we need them. That said, I've always used the rules as more of guidelines. Which is to say, I try to look at the WHY the rule is in place and enforce that, rather than the as written rule. Dietaku and CitanHyuga can probably tell you better, as they were in my (now defunct) live game. Its rarely had any mechanical impact on the game; the only time I can remember was when I had to stat out a human body as an improvised MA weapon, then next session we realized Infernals had already done it. I think it would probably be more accurate to say that I've always allowed stunts to run into rule-bendy territory. Take that as you will. Oh, and there's likely going to be plenty of combat, so as long as your character isn't solely focused on combat, you should be fine. <br /> <br /> Jim- I appreciate the concern, but make away! I have no expectations on anyone's characters (except Dietaku and CitanHyuga, but I know them and I know what types of characters they like to play, so its less of an expectation, and more of a prediction). I would much rather you build your characters to be in line with the other players than any vision I have for the game, since I've found that the inter-player, inter-PC dynamic is the most important one.<br /> <br /> As for the etiquette, just be polite and respectful, and you'll do fine. There is no universal Play-by-Post etiquette; each forum has its own nuances and code, but from what I've seen it all boils down to (1) Be excellent to each other, and (2) Have Fun. Plus, think of this: Since Onyx Path has no established PbP community, we are building the informal PbP code on this site. Isn't that pretty damn neat?<br /> <br /> Now, to the group at large. As I said, I'd rather you try to build your characters with each other than with me. At this time I'm going to plan on going ahead with the background I posted earlier. At current detail level, it should be enough to give you a foundation to build without locking you into anything in particular. With six players, there will be overlapping roles, so you'll probably be able to build a character into whatever role you desire, without the Circle being left in the lurch. That said, I do highly encourage collaboration in character building. Once you have your characters finished though, get them to me privately, either through PM or AIM. You can also contact me through those methods if you have any questions or concerns that you'd rather not level to the group at large.<br /> <br /> Alrighty, then! I look forward to what you come up with!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:12:49-08:00","id":43015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=42698#post42698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Jim- those ideas are all pretty cool, and all sound like they could be applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm gonna do something a little weird here: I'm going to give you a little more info on my character concepts, but I'm going to have odd blanks that are mostly for you to fill in according to the needs of your story. Like, remember who with the Full Moon concept, I said the kid's mom is a [demon/fae/ghost]? I was going to leave it up to you, or at least your input, to decide which kind of monster is more appropriate to your story or which one would call you the least trouble.<br /> <br /> Right. Off we go.<br /> <br /> <b>Jagger, beloved crimelord</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Jagger is a boss for [crime organization in the game's primary town] who started off as muscle and worked his way up to the top the hard way: by killing his boss when his boss asked Jagger to take the fall for a job gone bad. It was a dangerous move, but Jagger makes friends easily with his ability to keep his personal opinions to himself and his casual acts of kindness to support people around him, so he had enough support that the organization stayed in place despite the risk. The organization has done well under Jagger's command, though a lot of that is because he's willing to delegate responsibilities to those better equipped than he to handle them. The community is largely supportive of him because he makes his success theirs, taking care of his employees and their families as well as spreading his wealth around. The organization has pretty much moved out of local crime as to avoid alienating the community and is focused now mostly on importing illegal substances through a furniture shop Jagger owns an interest in after its owner got behind on gambling debts.<br /> <br /> Jagger is a good man. He's also a bad one. He's hurt and killed for no other reason than his own profit. Nevertheless, he has a moral compass he adheres to, and it earned him a powerful ally. Jagger always had a cat and mouse relationship with Dezino, an outcaste magistrate in [game's primary town] that Jagger kept ahead of mostly by knowing the limitations of Terrestrial lie-detecting Charms and being careful to always have a wall of deniability in front of everything, but one day a member of a rival criminal organization kidnapped Dezino's son. This outraged Jagger--children are <i>not</i> part of the game--and he turned the town upside down to find the kid. He shut down all of his businesses and paid his employees out of his own pocket for a week to get them in on the hunt, bankrupting himself in the process but finding the child. He Exalted for it, and it was a good thing, because Dezino had come into Jagger's office in a rage and beaten the crime boss within an inch of his life looking for proof of who had the boy, so an Exalted metabolism helped him heal his wounds with a lot less discomfort than he otherwise might have had. Returning the child did not make him Dezino's friend, but the Dragon-Blood knows he owes the criminal a lifelong favor now.<br /> <br /> After the kidnapping, the rival organization was destroyed by a Dragon-Blood on a vendetta, and Jagger controls pretty much all crime in town. He also knows he's capable of much, much more than that, but he doesn't know what to do with all his power. Divine right suggests he should perhaps start reshaping the world according to his own sense of right and wrong, and he could be okay with that--if nothing else, it would be a challenge--but he's been driven by risk analysis and personal profit for so long he's just not sure what to do with himself.<br /> <br /> As a character, Jagger is a pretty social-focused one. He knows his personal power is built on the support of those beneath him, and he takes care of them. He has a big supporting cast and will be reticent to leave them or the places where they're safe.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Yuma of the White, killer and hunted kingmaker</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yuma was born to a warrior caste in [I don't have a particular place in mind and would probably make one up if you have no ideas you want to use]. He was never a smart man, but he had a quick eye and he learned his lessons well. He was a good enough soldier to graduate to commando, and when he quit military service at age 38 after having spent most of his life as a grunt, he took a job as a bodyguard because spotting threats and killing people were pretty much the only skills he had, so his career options were limited to violent ones. So, ultimately, was his death: His own client ambushed him and killed him, yelling something about the client's wife. Yuma was never sure what the man was on about; he'd never touched the client's wife.<br /> <br /> Yuma is convinced he died and Luna saved him. No one has bothered arguing with him about it. Despite his fairly compelling reason to seek revenge, he's never done so, because Exaltation has changed him in ways he's not convinced are good ones. He's drawn as if compelled to [demons/fae/ghosts, whichever you'd prefer to work with], not with violent intent but with fascination. He's even sired a son with one, and he's now convinced he's cursed, possibly from this life but more likely from his previous one, to become a creature of darkness, a servant of some other, inimical world. It even shows in his Tell: Anyone can see his skin is pale, but those who pierce the Tell can see his skin is the color of [Malfean porcelain/ghost jade/gossamer].<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact found Yuma and assuaged his fears with a gift, a prayer piece Yuma calls Lead Merchant. As long as he can still use that, he is still pure, and he holds to it dearly. The Pact has more or less cut ties with him since the birth of his son came to light, and Yuma can live with that. He's on the run from the Pact and from anyone else who has an interest in hurting him or his half-human son, working odd jobs here and there to support them both while trying to give Chambers Appointed with Jade a good life. He's the boy's sole caregiver since his mother delivered him to Yuma in something of a panic, wanting him to live in a world less likely to eat him, and he is Yuma's entire reason for being.<br /> <br /> Yuma is a Prince of the Earth, but he has no idea what to do with that. If you gave him a kingdom, he'd probably turn it down as something he can't use. His son, though...his son is royalty in two worlds, and to Yuma's way of thinking, that means Chambers Appointed with Jade deserves to sit on a throne of his own. Yuma will make that happen...somehow. He doesn't know how. That's not really his skill set. He thinks he probably needs friends, which is hard for him; he's a hard man, suspicious of everyone and not prone to friendships, most likely to solve any problem by killing it as he was taught to. Learning peace has been very hard for him.<br /> <br /> Yuma is not a team player, but he's learning. He may be hard to get along with until he's as sure as he can be that no one means his boy any harm. His goals are to protect his son and the boy's mother (a boy needs his mother, is what Yuma thinks), and if anyone gets in his way...well, he knows how to get people out of his way.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This seems like it's probably about to hit the word limit for a post. I'll do another one in a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:58:48-08:00","id":43047,"title":"","content":"Jagger could fit into the rather simplistic view of the game I currently have very easily. I had more or less envisioned the nation as being structured similarly to a Hellenic City-State. There's a central Polis (the capital Novalesk) with a handful of of satellites that exist on the border of small city and large town, and a cloud of agricultural demes around each town/city. I could see him running crime in one of the satellite cities and its surrounding territory, since being the mafioso in the the central Polis would require WAY more background dots than are available at chargen. To flesh him out, I would suggest taking the Code of Honor Merit and either the Obligation Merit or Ally background.<br /> <br /> Yuma may be harder, but is still possible. Ghost or Fae would be easiest for me to integrate, because I've already added the dead and the Fae to the miniature three apocalypse pileup. That said, any of the three could work. I would suggest taking the Ally background for your spouse (depending on their power-level), and the Ward Flaw for your son. Now, I am envisioning the political system of Novalesk being an Essence-based oligarchy. The current succession conflict is occurring because the old ruler, a god-blooded daughter of the city-father, just achieved apotheosis. The strongest claimants are a middle-aged enlightened mortal, and a recently exalted DB. And the PCs, of course, but y'all will have to build your backing. <br /> <br /> I'm reminded of a few things. I am allowing the Merits and Flaws system in Scroll of Heroes, but they should all be justified as part of your backstory. Jagger serves as a good example of this, as illustrating that he has a Code of Honor (Don't harm children) and the story for how he received an Obligation. Also, I typically don't charge exp for backgrounds gained through play or good roleplaying. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T12:56:59-08:00","id":43074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43047#post43047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see him running crime in one of the satellite cities and its surrounding territory, since being the mafioso in the the central Polis would require WAY more background dots than are available at chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't know about that. Backing 5 (Polis Crime Syndicate), Contacts 3 (Beggar, Corrupt Cop, Merchant), Followers 3, Influence 2 - that would cost 8bp in addition to all your Background dots, but you have full control of the local criminal underworld, three major contacts and +3 dice for finding information, a hundred of &quot;elite soldiers&quot; level extras to act as your personal loyal troops, and everyone who matters knows your name... Doable, if expensive.<br /> <br /> RE: house rules; if this to be a mixed game involving Solars... Would it be possible to convince you to consider making the BP/xp costs paid by other splats the same as Solar costs? It's just kind of annoying to pay 10 bp for Essence 3 when a Solar pays only 7 for no real good reason. Just a consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T14:19:58-08:00","id":43126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43074#post43074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I don't know about that. Backing 5 (Polis Crime Syndicate), Contacts 3 (Beggar, Corrupt Cop, Merchant), Followers 3, Influence 2 - that would cost 8bp in addition to all your Background dots, but you have full control of the local criminal underworld, three major contacts and +3 dice for finding information, a hundred of &quot;elite soldiers&quot; level extras to act as your personal loyal troops, and everyone who matters knows your name... Doable, if expensive.<br /> <br /> RE: house rules; if this to be a mixed game involving Solars... Would it be possible to convince you to consider making the BP/xp costs paid by other splats the same as Solar costs? It's just kind of annoying to pay 10 bp for Essence 3 when a Solar pays only 7 for no real good reason. Just a consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot Resources 3-4 at least. But I'll concede the point. It is doable, albeit in an expensive manner. <br /> <br /> As for the house rule, I'll consider it. I'm going to have to look and see exactly what costs will be changed and how, but I'll get an answer to y'all as soon as I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:24:08-08:00","id":43163,"title":"","content":"I have a couple of ideas here, I think. <br /> <br /> First off, I've got a couple of Solar ideas. Chiyoko, a Zenith Caste who's basically inspired by Shrine Maidens in her look, at the very least. I was going to wait until 3e before really trying to find a game for her, but...<br /> <br /> Here's the pic I have of her. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i1015.photobucket.com/albums/af275/umbrellako2/547dfb45.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> (Artist is Kasanip from Giant in the Playground Forums)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The other idea I currently have is a Sidereal Exalted Chosen of Battles, who was a member of the Bronze Faction before falling in love with either a Solar or a Lunar, and changed her factional allegiance to either the Gold or Silver faction- depending, of course, on which Exalted type her lover is. Again, pic. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://static3.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20131117112938/typemoon/images/b/b1/SakuraSaber1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:50:50-08:00","id":43186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43074#post43074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RE: house rules; if this to be a mixed game involving Solars... Would it be possible to convince you to consider making the BP/xp costs paid by other splats the same as Solar costs? It's just kind of annoying to pay 10 bp for Essence 3 when a Solar pays only 7 for no real good reason. Just a consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back to this- after consideration, I will allow this. Henceforth, in this game all PC exalts will use the same base BP/xp costs. Note that I'm saying BASE cost. If a background or something says that it increases costs (like Mentor for Sidereals, or Cult for DBs) that modification still takes effect, but off of the cost as if you were a Solar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43163#post43163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a couple of ideas here, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, despite saying earlier that I had tentatively closed recruitment, I did so in a way that could cause confusion. Horngeek, you're in. Those do look like awesome ideas. I look forward to seeing how they'll play out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 02-16-2014, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:01:40-08:00","id":43191,"title":"","content":"Oh. Whoops. <br /> <br /> Anyway, Sakura's (that's the current name of the Sidereal idea) lover would preferably be a PC if I go that route- I'm not sure whether I'll go for Sakura or Chiyoko. <br /> <br /> The latter... well, I really do want to use that awesome character image, and she'd be very suited to a nation-building game (also, I have a firmer idea of Chiyoko's backstory). She's a former priestess of the goddess of a city in the general area of the Scavenger Lands- most likely one nearish Lookshy and very much aligned with it, which explains why she had to leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:02:18-08:00","id":43193,"title":"","content":"As much as I like my Sidereal idea, I just remembered how much I hate Arcane Fate and keeping track of resplendent destinies, so I'm probably gonna drop that idea. I'll try to come up with a replacement in a bit. I just don't feel like either of the ideas I have are particularly suited to the game at hand, so I will keep thinking.<br /> <br /> There is a fourth idea, one that began its life as an Infernal, but I can't figure out how to translate it to the splats allowed. The underlying idea is the son of a Dragon-Blood whose father gave up on him when the kid didn't Exalt, so the son decided to corrupt and destroy the Immaculate Faith because he felt the Dragons owed him an Exaltation. He Exalted as an Infernal and now has more power than any Dragon-Blood ever has or could, and he wants to use that power to get revenge on his father and take his place astride the world; but he's conflicted because his anger stems from wanting to please his dad, and there's still love in there, and he can't figure out what to do with it.<br /> <br /> The reason I'm having trouble translating this from an Infernal concept is the character is a monster in his own eyes, and he continues to be one not because it makes him happy but because his self-loathing is so reflexive it drives him to be something he hates. I think that is best expressed through an Infernal lens. I could do it with something else, but the son of a Dragon-Blood who becomes Anathema and has to deal with it is just...I don't know, I just can't figure out a way to do it that doesn't seem cliche and hokey. If you have any ideas on how to translate the concept to a permissible splat, I'd appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:36:52-08:00","id":43210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43191#post43191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. Whoops.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Sakura's (that's the current name of the Sidereal idea) lover would preferably be a PC if I go that route- I'm not sure whether I'll go for Sakura or Chiyoko.<br /> <br /> The latter... well, I really do want to use that awesome character image, and she'd be very suited to a nation-building game (also, I have a firmer idea of Chiyoko's backstory). She's a former priestess of the goddess of a city in the general area of the Scavenger Lands- most likely one nearish Lookshy and very much aligned with it, which explains why she had to leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do that, but it would require another Player to agree to integrate their back-story with yours... which would be their decision, not mine. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43193#post43193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I like my Sidereal idea, I just remembered how much I hate Arcane Fate and keeping track of resplendent destinies, so I'm probably gonna drop that idea. I'll try to come up with a replacement in a bit. I just don't feel like either of the ideas I have are particularly suited to the game at hand, so I will keep thinking.<br /> <br /> There is a fourth idea, one that began its life as an Infernal, but I can't figure out how to translate it to the splats allowed. The underlying idea is the son of a Dragon-Blood whose father gave up on him when the kid didn't Exalt, so the son decided to corrupt and destroy the Immaculate Faith because he felt the Dragons owed him an Exaltation. He Exalted as an Infernal and now has more power than any Dragon-Blood ever has or could, and he wants to use that power to get revenge on his father and take his place astride the world; but he's conflicted because his anger stems from wanting to please his dad, and there's still love in there, and he can't figure out what to do with it.<br /> <br /> The reason I'm having trouble translating this from an Infernal concept is the character is a monster in his own eyes, and he continues to be one not because it makes him happy but because his self-loathing is so reflexive it drives him to be something he hates. I think that is best expressed through an Infernal lens. I could do it with something else, but the son of a Dragon-Blood who becomes Anathema and has to deal with it is just...I don't know, I just can't figure out a way to do it that doesn't seem cliche and hokey. If you have any ideas on how to translate the concept to a permissible splat, I'd appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>He could very well be a Solar. Yeah. Allow me to elucidate.<br /> <br /> So, he gets pissed of with the Dragons cause he didn't Exalt. Then, he goes out and starts doing ridiculous things, to PROVE to the Dragons that he's strong/tough/cool/worthy enough to be an Exalt. And, it turns out that he is, so the Unconquered Sun exalts him. Now, from what you said, it made it seem like he did believe in the Immaculate Philosophy, he just hated it for &quot;abandoning&quot; him. Now, if he exalts as a Solar, he would become, in his mind, a Demon. The worst sort of monster imaginable. Even as he learns that the Immaculate Philosophy is incorrect, his strict religious upbringing plants a seed in his subconscious mind that his power, no matter how he uses it, is deeply, fundamentally <i>wrong.</i>The fact that he's allying with other Anathema could be enough to give him a strong sense of disquiet. <br /> <br /> That's how I would do it, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:57:32-08:00","id":43227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43193#post43193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I'm having trouble translating this from an Infernal concept is the character is a monster in his own eyes, and he continues to be one not because it makes him happy but because his self-loathing is so reflexive it drives him to be something he hates. I think that is best expressed through an Infernal lens. I could do it with something else, but the son of a Dragon-Blood who becomes Anathema and has to deal with it is just...I don't know, I just can't figure out a way to do it that doesn't seem cliche and hokey. If you have any ideas on how to translate the concept to a permissible splat, I'd appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually considering running my Lunar as a Dynastic Scion myself (House Ledaal, Represent) who exalted as a Lunar while desperately trying to prove to the Dragons that she was worthy by going on suicidal pilgrimages to Ledaal family temple-shrines in the Scavenger Lands. Her divided loyalties to her new-found mentor and the Silver pact and her House was going to be a main contention of conflict for her, but also provide a sense of unique perspective. For instance, she's influenced by Realm tactics and mannerisms, and is not totally bigoted to DBs. Indeed, one of her plans for her Thousand Streams River experiment is to prove to her peers that cultivating DBs within a nation isn't a recipe for disaster.<br /> <br /> That said, I really enjoy the synergy of GSPs and the betrayal that being a discovered Anathema within the Scarlet Dynasty provides. I'd really enjoy seeing that work. While its not up to me, I wouldn't mind. However, be warend: I did something similar, in my last game, where I played a Slayer who was found newly returned from her training and not entirely certain on her loyalties, and decided to play the field a bit. This earned her a Sidereal &quot;Parole Officer&quot; and a lot of supervision from the Gold Faction. (This really wasn't as bad as it sounds. It kinda developed into a buddy cop situation whereby my parole officer and I rampaged across Hell and generally got into mischief in the South-East.) However, should you go this route, I imagine such a situation will be presented to you.<br /> <br /> @Fallen Ecco: Thanks, I appreciate that. Let's all take a moment to mourn that which has passed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":". 01-05-2014, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T19:06:37-08:00","id":43278,"title":"","content":"I only saved a sliver...many things were lost forever...including several Yozi/Infernal charm sets.<br /> I did get 3 or 4 ones for the Black Boar though ^^<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to topic, I'm having a little trouble dealing with Glass Walker (the Eclipse I'm trying to build.). There are a couple of bits in his back-story that I feel need to be fleshed out more, and I don't seem to have enough Charms. But seeing as how I did not see him as much of a fighter, (more of a deal-maker) the lack of a perfect defense doesn't bother me much. Given the nnumber of people coming from the Realm though, I'm not sure if I need a Contact there anymore.<br /> <br /> Concept pic (Spearman by Anto Juricic) <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.3dartistonline.com/users/2224/thm1024/1335374505_spearman_render_S.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\">I admit, it looks more like a DB than a Solar, but it fits the image in my head.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 01-05-2014, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T12:24:48-08:00","id":43651,"title":"","content":"@Horngeek: I'm down for having my Lunar being your Siddie's special someone, if you're okay with an &quot;open&quot; relationship. I like the Solar priestess concept, too, though. That's a neat picture.<br /> <br /> @FallenEco: I'm having the same issue, albeit with a lack of neat persuasion tricks AND having a basic DBT suite. Also, your choice of weapons is neat. Dire Lances need love, too. I wouldn't be too worried about having any PDs, as I ran a Lunar in one of Noodle's games without one for the entire chronicle. <br /> <br /> I have my back-story ironed out. I'll post it next time, though. I'm running low on time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:50:29-08:00","id":43708,"title":"","content":"@Dietaku: That would actually be EXTREMELY interesting, given Sakura's concept as ex-Bronze faction. There'd be a possibility of the pair trying to find a 'middle ground' so to speak between the Realm, returning Solars and the Lunars (although Chiyoko would be down for something like that too- she's very much about proving the Solars don't have to be monsters). And yes, Sakura would be fine with an 'open' relationship.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Sakura...<br /> <br /> ...oh. Um.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have a copy of Wind-Cutting Blade Style hanging around somewhere? Now the Wiki's gone, it's... kinda gone too. And Sakura was going to be using that style.<br /> <br /> Chiyoko's easier, she uses Crane Style with some Solar Hero style (incidentally, my fanon 'formalised name' for that one is Fist of the Daystar Style).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:52:50-08:00","id":43711,"title":"","content":"Hey Horngeek, are you leaning toward the Zenith idea? Omicron mentioned thinking he and I could have some character synergy if I ran with my Zenith, and I'd like to know if I need to start altering things (he could be an Eclipse without too much work...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:57:56-08:00","id":43712,"title":"","content":"Currently, I'm flip-flopping between the two. Let me just pull up your Zenith Concept- after all, two members of the same Caste can be very different. <br /> <br /> ...given your Zenith idea has the concept of 'Mafia Don', I imagine they will be anyway. Actually, the idea of the two Zeniths with (I imagine) VERY different outlooks interacting is starting to lean me towards Chiyoko. :P<br /> <br /> But yeah. I could, potentially, build Sakura with Violet Bier of Sorrows Style, but I'd rather not if I can find a copy of Wind-Cutting Blade Style. That might be enough to cross her out if I can't find WCBS, to be honest (although Dietaku, Chiyoko and your Lunar could still have a very interesting interplay, given that Chiyoko rather likes the base concept of the Realm).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T15:33:15-08:00","id":43754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43712#post43712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently, I'm flip-flopping between the two. Let me just pull up your Zenith Concept- after all, two members of the same Caste can be very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The main conceit behind Jagger as a character for me is whom is chosen to be a Solar. Lunars are chosen from survivors; Sidereals are chosen from those destined to learn the importance of this or that aspect of fate; Dragon-Blooded are chosen from those who have enough of the right blood. Solars are chosen from leaders. I wanted to play with that idea, with how someone who is chosen to be a priest-king controlling the hearts and faith of the multitudes could have gained the skills and qualifications for that role without having the nobility one would think would be inherent to such a figure.<br /> <br /> I ended up with a mafioso.<br /> <br /> I just like playing with a game's expectations, and that's where Jagger came from. I can still play with expectations some by making him an Eclipse--Eclipses value harmony, and Jagger values harmony more than most because, as a criminal, he knows discord is both hard on the organization's bank accounts and dangerous for the organization's employees--but I think it's more fun as a Zenith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43712#post43712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could, potentially, build Sakura with Violet Bier of Sorrows Style, but I'd rather not if I can find a copy of Wind-Cutting Blade Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that style sexy? I love it. Just in case you didn't know, though, not real long before the old forums died, Holden kind of disavowed it, saying it wasn't very good. He didn't explain why, which bummed me out (it also bummed me out that no one ever updated it for Alchemicals and Infernals), but I just thought you should know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T15:45:35-08:00","id":43764,"title":"","content":"I respectfully disagree with Holden on this matter. :P<br /> <br /> But yeah, I don't have a copy of it saved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T16:00:08-08:00","id":43771,"title":"","content":"I have narrowed down my concept some.<br /> <br /> The character is a Sidereal, Chosen of Journey/Serenity (probably the latter), who wears a Revelation Blindfold at all times. Her cover identity is that of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goze\" target=\"_blank\">goze</a>, a wandering blind musician, though many who know her understand that she is actually an advisor of some kind to the powerful who can hire her. In truth, she is a member of a Gold Faction, sent to the Hundred Kingdoms to survey and advise a newborn Solar (current plans are that he be JimB's character), and to help strengthen the region as it faces outsider forces.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, aside from always-on AESS, the character would mostly have a social and martial focus. She has Performance and Presence Charms, and tries to influence people subtly without them realizing it... Or she brings out the kickass against those who prove too much of a hurdle.<br /> <br /> At this point I am mostly stuck on elements of aesthetics and choice of style. I could have her use Artifact war fans with Crane Style (she would probably be a technical pacifist who punches people to teach them to be better persons), I could have her be an unarmed singer using Silver-Voiced Nightingale and playing an Unsurpassed Sanxian, or I could have her be an Ivory Pestle Stylist wielding an Artifact staff/flute and using ghost-slaying Charms to put the dead to rest; the country seems like it might need it.<br /> <br /> I am not sure which would be best/coolest. I am also toying with the idea of her having the Oathbound merit as a representation of her devotion to the Maidens having led her to take a specific vow that restricts her behavior. Not sure which, though.<br /> <br /> Any opinion/advice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T16:31:17-08:00","id":43786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43771#post43771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically, aside from always-on AESS, the character would mostly have a social and martial focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Telltale Symphony makes me wish I like playing Sidereals more than I do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43771#post43771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have her use Artifact war fans with Crane Style (she would probably be a technical pacifist who punches people to teach them to be better persons), I could have her be an unarmed singer using Silver-Voiced Nightingale and playing an Unsurpassed Sanxian, or I could have her be an Ivory Pestle Stylist wielding an Artifact staff/flute and using ghost-slaying Charms to put the dead to rest; the country seems like it might need it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dig Crane Style, though I will point out just to tempt you that it seems like a missed opportunity to have this many Celestial Exalted in the party and <i>not</i> do Throne Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T16:34:12-08:00","id":43787,"title":"","content":"Also, if I go for Chiyoko, Crane Style will be a martial art she goes into, although I'm not sure if she'll /start/ with Crane Style Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T16:47:20-08:00","id":43796,"title":"","content":"Argh Throne Shadow Style, why must you be such an obvious choice? But you don't allow for war fans and quarterstaffs! Only brawling aids. And my Sidereal musician can't very well wear god-kicking boots now can she? Or maybe she can. <br /> <br /> I don't know any mooooore<br /> <br /> Crane Style is cool and I like it. It also offers amazing interactions with Compassionate Essence Replenishment. My only annoyance is that it doesn't synergize well with Smooth Transition, which I might want to take to deal with ghosts and Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T17:29:03-08:00","id":43815,"title":"","content":"I did not manage to save any of the Martial Arts from the wiki. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Not that this is very relevant, but I think I should put it out there just in case it's useful. Willow (at the moment) is a widower with an estranged child, (keep flip-flopping on the gender). They fell out before Willow Exalted, so that will be interesting. In case it isn't obvious, Glass Willow is meant to be an older individual. He shaves his head to hide his bald patch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I intend for Glass Willow to have his own &quot;business consulting firm&quot;, even if he was the first to invent one. It's something to do rather than retire. He is also meant to be a negotiator, not a persuader. No UMI.<br /> <br /> @Dietaku: Thank You! Dire Lances do need more love and your advice helped a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T17:39:16-08:00","id":43823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43796#post43796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Argh Throne Shadow Style, why must you be such an obvious choice? But you don't allow for war fans and quarterstaves! Only brawling aids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was there ever actually a Charm to declare any random object to be a Throne Shadow form weapon, or am I making that up?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43796#post43796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And my Sidereal musician can't very well wear god-kicking boots now can she? Or maybe she can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't tell if I love or hate the idea of a Sidereal with starmetal tap shoes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43796#post43796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crane Style is cool and I like it. It also offers amazing interactions with Compassionate Essence Replenishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43796#post43796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only annoyance is that it doesn't synergize well with Smooth Transition, which I might want to take to deal with ghosts and Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>For as much as it's worth, it sounds like we'll have at least one Zenith on board, and that may obviate a lot of the need for Smooth Transition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T17:44:19-08:00","id":43826,"title":"","content":"Question to the group: We got anyone planning to do sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T17:53:28-08:00","id":43831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43764#post43764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I respectfully disagree with Holden on this matter. :P<br /> <br /> But yeah, I don't have a copy of it saved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't found any copy of it, either. I'll keep looking, but I think you should consider other options in the meantime. If you'd like, we could try making a thematically appropriate CMA. Alternatively, I could try to get in contact with one of my old STs about a Sword-based &quot;Storm&quot;-themed CMA he made for another game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43796#post43796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Argh Throne Shadow Style, why must you be such an obvious choice? But you don't allow for war fans and quarterstaffs! Only brawling aids. And my Sidereal musician can't very well wear god-kicking boots now can she? Or maybe she can.<br /> <br /> I don't know any mooooore<br /> <br /> Crane Style is cool and I like it. It also offers amazing interactions with Compassionate Essence Replenishment. My only annoyance is that it doesn't synergize well with Smooth Transition, which I might want to take to deal with ghosts and Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played a fair number of Throne Shadow practitioners. The Sidereal &quot;Parole Officer&quot; that Dietaku mentioned? Yeah, that was one of my PCs, a Throne Shadow Stylist named Ascendant Sword. one thing that struck me as odd was that its form weapons only included brawling aids. I'd be inclined to allow war-fans and quarterstaves as form weapons, since I could very well see the elderly adviser or delicate courtier using the tools and accessories of the Court to kick someone's ass. That's part of the style's aesthetics, right? Or have I been reading that wrong the whole time?<br /> <br /> Either way, I am now getting many amusing images of Jafar beating the tar out of Aladdin with his staff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T17:54:05-08:00","id":43833,"title":"","content":"W<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as there ever actually a Charm to declare any random object to be a Throne Shadow form weapon, or am I making that up? </div> </div> </div>Not quite; World-As-Weapon Mastery allows you to treat shadow fingers as your &quot;weapons,&quot; that is to say to use your Throne Shadow Charms through them.<br /> <br /> However, being a Hero style, TS allows improvised weapons as form weapons anyway.<br /> <br /> Hm. Sorcery is good for kingdom-building.<br /> <br /> Tell you what: if no one has sorcery, I will shift my Sidereal from Martial Arts to Sorcerer. Then she'll be even more of a Vizier. With a magic staff. And a cape. <a href=\"http://i199.photobucket.com/albums/aa315/SeeNoReasonToSmile/Fate%20stay%20night%20and%20Zero/Caster/Caster11.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Which will fly.</a><br /> <br /> Because I can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's part of the style's aesthetics, right? Or have I been reading that wrong the whole time? </div> </div> </div>You have been reading it very right, good sir, and I applaud you for it.<br /> <br /> Now I want to be a sorcerer/martial artist combining Throne Shadow with Jaffar-style magical staff. And blastospells. Sadly I'll never have enough points. Must focus!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 01-06-2014, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:00:27-08:00","id":43838,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's looking more and more like Chiyoko will be my entered character for this, not Sakura. On the other hand, Dietaku, Chiyoko could always be your character's Solar Mate- the interplay would still be pretty fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:08:44-08:00","id":43846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43823#post43823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there ever actually a Charm to declare any random object to be a Throne Shadow form weapon, or am I making that up?</div> </div> </div> </div>The capstone makes any attack from your shadow fingers count as Form Weapons (make all members of circle Shadow Fingers+Horrific Wreath+World as Weapon Mastery=Profit).<br /> <br /> There's a charm that allows you to add a Form Weapon to any style you've mastered- its a Charm called Master's Hand Envisioned Anew in Dreams of the First age 2, p 157. The only errata on it is the clarification that the new form weapons must make sense for the style. The example they give is that a crossbow would be a valid addition to Wood Dragon, but not Snake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:11:08-08:00","id":43849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43787#post43787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I go for Chiyoko, Crane Style will be a martial art she goes into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me know which character you settle on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:21:30-08:00","id":43854,"title":"","content":"Given that Wind-Cutting Blade Style is looking like a bust, I'm going for Chiyoko.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:26:15-08:00","id":43860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43833#post43833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Sorcery is good for kingdom-building.<br /> <br /> Tell you what: if no one has sorcery, I will shift my Sidereal from Martial Arts to Sorcerer. Then she'll be even more of a Vizier. With a magic staff. And a cape. <a href=\"http://i199.photobucket.com/albums/aa315/SeeNoReasonToSmile/Fate%20stay%20night%20and%20Zero/Caster/Caster11.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Which will fly.</a><br /> <br /> Because I can.<br /> <br /> Now I want to be a sorcerer/martial artist combining Throne Shadow with Jaffar-style magical staff. And blastospells. Sadly I'll never have enough points. Must focus!</div> </div> </div> </div>Caster would make an excellent Sidereal. Hmmm. If you want a flying cape, Brightly Shattered Ice (Arianna's First age incarnation) had one in her write-up in Dreams. Might be worth a look. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:48:47-08:00","id":43879,"title":"","content":"I shouldn't have started playing Fate/unlimited code, now I want to make every Servant.<br /> <br /> Apparently BSI's flying cape is a Wings of the Raptor, 4-dot Artifact from WotLA. Which are pretty cool all considered.<br /> <br /> Argh. Choices. Subtle Throne Shadow Stylist with war fans, or blatant flying sorceress with magic staff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 01-06-2014, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T19:20:46-08:00","id":43893,"title":"","content":"Well, Sakura has one of the (many) Sabers as her character pic. Really, Fate/whatever is a brilliant source for Exalted character images.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T19:32:04-08:00","id":43897,"title":"","content":"I'm going to back out. Got a lot on my plate right now with school just starting. Apparently I chose two heavy work-load classes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/922-hailey-mcauliffe","name":"Hailey McAuliffe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T20:53:25-08:00","id":43933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hailey McAuliffe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43897#post43897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to back out. Got a lot on my plate right now with school just starting. Apparently I chose two heavy work-load classes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, that really sucks. Well, best of luck with your studies. Consider yourself to have an open invitation to return, if and when your study schedule allows. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horngeek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43893#post43893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Sakura has one of the (many) Sabers as her character pic. Really, Fate/whatever is a brilliant source for Exalted character images.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I once made a Night Caste NPC that I used EMIYA Archer as a jumping off point for. Once he actually entered the game though, I realized that I ended up going full circle, and roughly back at my starting point, in terms of evolving him past the concept. When I realized this, I moved him away, thematically and mechanically, but the seed was still there. A combination of his unmodified stealth dice pool of 13 and the fact that the players and I kept forgetting that he was running around with the Circle led to the running gag that he was so stealthy that he emulated Arcane Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T23:50:16-08:00","id":43988,"title":"","content":"Heh. There's one character I've been building ideas up for for <i>ages</i>. She's actually developed into Shoat of the Mire (like, literally- the question I'd ask any ST if I was interested putting this character idea into their game was 'this character is pretty much Shoat of the Mire gone renegade. Can I just go ahead and make her Shoat?') with Redemption as a specific goal for her both IC and OOC (doesn't quite fit into a Nation-Building game even if you were allowing Abyssals- even with the Doom rules instead of 'standard' Resonance, Abyssals have trouble with that type of game for... obvious reasons).<br /> <br /> But once she does attain Redemption, I'd basically use an image of Saber Lily for her character pic.<br /> <br /> Aaaaanyway. I'd better start writing Chiyoko up in terms of character sheet and write down her fluff into a coherent form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","user":"horngeek","date":". 01-07-2014, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T23:57:47-08:00","id":43990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43879#post43879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I shouldn't have started playing Fate/unlimited code, now I want to make every Servant.<br /> <br /> Apparently BSI's flying cape is a Wings of the Raptor, 4-dot Artifact from WotLA. Which are pretty cool all considered.<br /> <br /> Argh. Choices. Subtle Throne Shadow Stylist with war fans, or blatant flying sorceress with magic staff?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's simple. What would you have more fun with this time?<br /> If need be someone else can pick up Sorcery, so don't feel you have to do it. Either way, it's going to be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T00:28:06-08:00","id":44008,"title":"","content":"Hold the presses, I have an idea that changes everything.<br /> <br /> Open your Wonders of the Lost Age p.157.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unyielding Fury of Righteousness was the red jade warstrider gifted by Chejop Kejak to the Scarlet Empress herself, Forged in her effigy and never used, it was stored in a crate and forgotten by all. Until today.<br /> <br /> In the wake of the Empress's disappearance, a group of Dynasts feeling the approach of a civil war and wanting to secure an overwhelming asset found the paper trail of the relic and set up the heist of many centuries. Dragon-Blooded and loyal mortal retainers gathered to steal into the winter palace of Arjuf and make off with Fury. One of these mortals was a young red-haired girl of Fire Aspect, here to assist her older brother.<br /> <br /> Of course, once inside the palace things went sour. The Dragon-Blooded turned on each other in their desire to take the wonder for themselves, and the sorcerous safeties of the place turned on them. Hounded by spirits and their own brothers, mortals and Exalts died one by one. The young Fire Aspect managed to find her way to the warsrider's crate and open it along with her brother, but while she was desperately rushing to reactivate it and open its piloting compartment a whirling cloud of blades killed him and left her alone. Blazing red hot with Essence and excitation, the girl managed to reactivate the Artifact...<br /> <br /> Waking up a confused and sleepy AI who mistook her for her original owner and happily offered her full control of Fury. The girl escaped in a blaze of fire and jade, and immediately started running for her life. She hasn't stopped; in fact, her desperate trek led her to the middle of the Scavenger Lands, where she offers her service as a warstrider pilot and hopes to delay the moment when the Realm finally catches up to her. She doesn't consider herself a traitor, but she does not believe anyone would stop long enough to listen to her explanations. So she runs, going from kingdom to kingdom and building up a new legend.<br /> <br /> Because she is a fiery-haired Dragon-Blooded piloting a legendary red jade warstrider depicting a very well-known woman, and her AI isn't the only one to have leaped to certain unfortunate conclusions. She has even taken to naming herself &quot;Scarlet,&quot; which she swears is a direct translation of her original High Realm name. The AI likes it, at least. </div> </div> </div>Character could alternatively be a mortal flunky who Exalted as a Night Caste.<br /> <br /> Provided you agree to the concept in the first place XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 01-07-2014, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T08:34:00-08:00","id":44185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=44008#post44008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold the presses, I have an idea that changes everything.<br /> <br /> Open your Wonders of the Lost Age p.157.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Character could alternatively be a mortal flunky who Exalted as a Night Caste.<br /> <br /> Provided you agree to the concept in the first place XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the concept in theory, but I worry about the cost...<br /> <br /> UFR is a Royal Warstrider. Which means 5 artifact dots. With a 5-dot integrated flight system, a medium Essence cannon (3 dots), a warstrider reaver daiklaive and powerbow (Artifact 2 each), that gets you to a total of 17 points in artifact, without even considering the AI is a 5-dot version, or the three dot hearthstone required to get the warstrider to operation. I'd allow you to remove any of the add-ons (due to them either being lost or damage beyond current capabilities to repair), but that still leaves Artifact 5, Integrated AI Ally 5, Manse 3. At the very least. <br /> <br /> So, its doable, but expensive. I would rather steal the warstrider in-game than do it in my backstory, personally. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T08:45:12-08:00","id":44193,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm. Let's see. Say the Es<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">sence cannon has been lost on the way...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Manse \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf (One 5-dot, one 3-dot, one 2-dot)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Artifact \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf (Unyielding Fury of Righteousness 5, Flight Systems 5)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">AI \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Artifact \u25cf\u25cf (Warstrider Daiklave 2, Warstrider Powerbow 2)<br /> <br /> That costs a total 12 BP: 4 to get Manse 5, 4 to get Artifact 5, 4 to get AI 5. Of course, that's only thanks to the Dynast background, which might not allowed for a character on the run.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> The real problem is that this leaves me with an Essence 2, Breeding 0 Dragon-Blood, which is hilariously punishing. On the other hand, flying giant mecha of doom. With its own Charms and friendly spirit ally. And a 5-dot Hearthstone to power its flight systems (yes, they require a HS equal to their rating). But I don't have enough to pay for an ally able to <i>maintain </i>UFR. Oh, and also, this costs 33m to attune. <br /> <br /> Mostly this makes me want to punch canon warstrider rules in the goddamn face.<br /> <br /> Doable. Restrictive, but doable. The real problem with stealing the warstrider in-game is that it essentially hijacks the story, as it's pretty much a plot of its own.<br /> <br /> Well, now I have three different, almost-complete sheets. Hard to choose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 01-07-2014, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T08:59:29-08:00","id":44207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=43826#post43826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question to the group: We got anyone planning to do sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't planned on it.<br /> <br /> @Horngeek: <br /> <img src=\"http://i880.photobucket.com/albums/ac10/Dietaku/bestfriends.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I'd be happy to have my character be Chiyoko's Lunar mate.<br /> <br /> I also find it rather hilarious that many, myself included, are thinking about going into MA as their fighting style. Granted mine is &quot;Lunar Native Dexterity Charms+MA as the ability,&quot; but still.<br /> <br /> And, as promised, here is my Lunar's back-story.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ledaal Monos Tirien, the eldest child of a middling lineage of the Ledaal family, desperately wanted to exalt. However, time and her siblings all receiving the Second Breath caused her to fall into despair that she'd be stuck as a mere Patrician. Therefore, she set out to prove her worthiness to Mela This prompted a series of pilgrimages to various temples to the Dragons in the Scavenger Lands. This resulted in a disaster when the No Moon Lunar, Mejan Holof, attacked the caravan she was part of. Forced to flee into the wilderness, lest she fall to the predations of the Anathema. There, the urbane Tirien had to learn first-hand how to survive in the wilderness for a month, as she wandered fruitlessly until coming in out of the wilderness to that Ur-City; Nexus. Guided by the Silver Horned Watcher, and imbued with the spirit shape of a great Marsupial Lion, Tierien managed to find her way once more. Mejan Holof appeared to her just as she entered the city, this time recognizing her as a fellow Steward. From there, he took her under his wing, training her in the ways of the Chosen of Luna. Now, Tirien is ready to take her teachings to heart and make an impact on the Threshold.<br /> <br /> <br /> A tall woman with many of the traits that mark her as Mela's descendant, Ledaal Tirien is very much a product of her homeland; proud, shrewd, and vain. However, she also is something of an eccentric. She enjoys learning of the First Age, and is something of an armchair general; being an avid Gateway and Goremaul RY535 player (One of her chief frustrations is that her family surely has boxed her precious Tepet Legion figurines. And she spent so long to get Arada and Ejava to look right...) Finally, while many in her position would be awash in grief, having become a monster in their eyes, Tirien is more relieved than anything, convinced that Mela withheld Her Blessing to allow Luna to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, attracted to the chaos of Novalesk by the tugging of her soul towards her Solar Mate, Chiyoko, Tierien figures this is as good a place as any to begin her Experiment.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T10:08:55-08:00","id":44261,"title":"","content":"@Omnicron- Given the restrictive nature of the DB+UFR build I would advise against it. Not saying I won't let you do it, just saying I doubt it would be a good idea, since you would end up having little utility outside of mass-combat situations, and that could make the game boring for you. Something to ponder. <br /> <br /> @Dietaku- Looking good.<br /> <br /> Okay a reminder to everyone: Once you have finished your character, get it to me PRIVATELY, however you'd like. That way, I can give it a look over and give final approval, and you can post as much or as little you'd like on your character in the OOC thread, which I will be starting as soon as I get the first finished character. <br /> <br /> Some other administrative things. I am not sure how y'all want to deal with the mechanical end of the house, during play. I've heard of situations where the ST retained all control over dice rolls, but I think that as limiting your freedom as players. This is how I propose to deal with things, and how things were dealt with in the myriad of PbP games I've been in. You retain direct control over rolling dice and activating charms for your character, unless you give me a contingency, which I will activate if applicable (ex: If you say &quot;If the Abyssal with the sword attacks me before my next action, I'll activate Crimson Palm Counterstrike in response&quot;, I'll activate the charm, roll the dice, etc. for your character if the Abyssal with the sword attacks you). Otherwise, I'll apply the results of your rolled actions to your targets, roll any NPC actions, and then tell you the result (&quot;The Abyssal's lunge will connect, and would deal 15L raw damage. Do you respond?&quot;) I know this messes up a large part of the step-based combat system, but I feel that doing otherwise would either slow the game to a crawl or force you try and give me dozens of potential contingencies, and neither of those outcomes are fun. If no-one has any objections, that's how it will go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:02:07-08:00","id":44291,"title":"","content":"I am having the damnedest time coming up with a good character concept. Or, well, good ones that are also applicable to the situation; for instance, Indiana-Jones-as-a-Solar doesn't have much to do with the kingdom-building plot (and I don't like focusing on Artifacts anyway).<br /> <br /> Hm. Someone who's a direct servant of the polis, maybe, who has a vested interest in building a kingdom. A courtier or spy or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:30:42-08:00","id":44314,"title":"","content":"I have, at least, settled on a concept: I am going to play the fan-wielding Crane Stylist Sidereal who's in it because ohmygad Solars everywhere need to keep all this in check. <br /> <br /> Now I need a good backstory. <br /> <br /> Also my character is basically Rider wearing flowing robes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:02:31-08:00","id":44339,"title":"","content":"Omicron, if you're going with your Sidereal, then I'm definitely going Solar. I really like your idea of guiding a Solar to do something actually worthwhile with his life, and if the offer is still open, I want to be a part of it. Maybe I can do...I'm thinking of kind of a spy/criminal for hire type who is realizing he's better than the work he does but feels trapped by his own lifestyle and doesn't know how to expand himself into the leader Creation needs him to be, and who latches onto your character because, shit, it's hard to get more noble than the idea of serving the will of Heaven (he doesn't know how ignoble and fractured Heaven actually is). Probably a Night, but maybe an Eclipse. I'm not specifically inspired by Amarant from <b>Final Fantasy IX</b>, but since I've been playing the game lately, he's the first example to spring to mind of the kind of personality I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> ...Although now that I mention Amarant, a spiritual killer, like a monkish assassin...I could get behind that...An old warrior who saw his end coming and wanted a final test of his skills, so he accepted a do or die contract against some supernatural being who should have been out of his league, like a Dragon-Blood or something, and he Exalted for it...<br /> <br /> I am excited about this idea. Let me know what you think, Omi, and everyone else too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 01-07-2014, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:30:34-08:00","id":44363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=44339#post44339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Although now that I mention Amarant, a spiritual killer, like a monkish assassin...I could get behind that...An old warrior who saw his end coming and wanted a final test of his skills, so he accepted a do or die contract against some supernatural being who should have been out of his league, like a Dragon-Blood or something, and he Exalted for it...<br /> <br /> I am excited about this idea. Let me know what you think, Omi, and everyone else too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this would be an awesome idea. Bonus points if a gold Faction Sidereal was tilted the dice in your favor a couple of times in your life, and surprise, they're also Omi's sidereal's Sifu (hence why you're a team). If you did that, you could get either the Mentor or Sifu background for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:15:45-08:00","id":44391,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty great idea! I'm all for it.<br /> <br /> I am not going to buy Sifu though, for... philosophical reasons. (I haaaate that Background). Maybe the mentor is too distant or busy to take care of Sea of Tears (that's my Sidereal's name, by the way) at the moment; he dropped her off with mission orders and is unavailable. Which, actually, could be why he sent her there in the first place - something came up that distracted him from his Solar &quot;pet project.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sea's Motivation is &quot;Spread love and peace through superior firepower.&quot; By which I mean beating people up with Crane Style and hammering the love of Creation into them. She could pair pretty well with a character who has a naive vision of Heaven because she's rather idealistic herself.<br /> <br /> I am considering starting the game with an Ascending Destiny of an illegal rating. You know, those Frequency 4 &quot;occurs every time its trigger is met&quot; things, which Sea hoped to slip by the Pattern Spiders unnoticed. Nothing game-breaking - a -1 TN to some kind of roll, perhaps (like what Simple Astrology does as its standard effect). Would that be a Dark Secret?<br /> <br /> Also, my sheet is almost done. I just need a presentable backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:52:01-08:00","id":44418,"title":"","content":"Real quick: May I ask what everyone plans to focus their characters on, in a broad sense? My guy (I haven't named him yet) could go a lot of different routes, go physical to be a brawler or social to be an infiltrator or mental to be the kind of guy who gets the job done by learning everything about it, so I thought I'd ask what areas need shoring up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:12:33-08:00","id":44428,"title":"","content":"Broadly: Sidereal Performance (binding spirits, &quot;soft&quot; social influence), Presence (subtle but &quot;hard&quot; social influence), kicking ass in an elegant and merciful manner (Crane Style makes it hard to kill anything). Later branching into Resistance. Don't be fooled by my Craft rating: the system is such a glorious mess, I will at best buy just enough to get Elemental Vision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:14:42-08:00","id":44434,"title":"","content":"@JimB: I'm aiming to be a warlord of sorts. Tirien will have a suite of DBT charms, training, and persuasion charms to make people amenable to her. I also plan to dabble a bit in infiltration insofar that being a Lunar and being sneaky isn't that hard, and the Charisma warfare charms are more about being sneaky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:35:59-08:00","id":44443,"title":"","content":"Sounds like social is pretty well covered, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:42:41-08:00","id":44447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=44418#post44418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real quick: May I ask what everyone plans to focus their characters on, in a broad sense? My guy (I haven't named him yet) could go a lot of different routes, go physical to be a brawler or social to be an infiltrator or mental to be the kind of guy who gets the job done by learning everything about it, so I thought I'd ask what areas need shoring up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chiyoko's very much a leader- she'll have Charm purchases in all the Zenith Abilites, at least, although not so much Survival. Some Socialise/Socialize (bah, American English), not sure what other abilities she'll have but I suspect Bureaucracy is in there even if she has no Charms there at start. Overall, she's a 'face' character who gets by on 'I honestly want the best for all involved'. Yes, she has a Compassion-based Limit Break. I'm thinking a custom one that removes her capacity for mercy, right now. <br /> <br /> On Lunar Martial Arts: You actually have a point there, Die- Lunar Hero Style sucks royally, but Lunars don't really <i>need</i> their own Martial Arts Style as Attribute-based Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:51:48-08:00","id":44454,"title":"","content":"Heh. I kind of want to go Disco Ninja Style for my guy, but I think we have up close and personal taken care of. Maybe something ranged. I never had much use for Thrown, but it fits a killer's style...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:18:58-08:00","id":44517,"title":"","content":"Okay all, I started the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\">OOC Thread</a>. Once you have your character finished, please post as brief description there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:34:04-08:00","id":44528,"title":"","content":"So, here is <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/16FB4t9EQhCVQ9nocUdsQzUc_LOvlUHs2q0d0bFnIxQQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Sea of Tears, Chosen of Serenity!</a><br /> <br /> Summed up quickly: she's a Joybringer who's grown desensitized to the exotic pleasures and wonders of the Cerulean Lute. She tries to teach people to be better persons by influence both subtle and overt, and she has some kind of standing bet with Venus of an unclear nature. She's been sent into the Threshold recently to watch over (probably Jim's Solar). She has fans, a blindfold and a silken armor, and the Backing of one faction and one division, giving her a lot of cool stuff.<br /> <br /> Being unable to raise Abilities above 3 without BP is an eternal annoyance, and I still need to find something to remove somewhere to come into my BP allotment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T10:03:46-08:00","id":45680,"title":"","content":"So, what's up with everyone's sheets/characters? Any concerns or questions or things to share?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T11:50:53-08:00","id":45744,"title":"","content":"Sorry it's taking me so long. Work's been a bitch lately, and I've spent a shameful amount of time just lying in bed on a heating pad. I'll get something cooked up soon; my biggest stumbling point right now is figuring out a style for this guy. Not, like, a martial arts style, but just a methodology. Since I haven't hear anything from CitanHyuga since this thread started, I might rework my dude to be a Twilight spy rather than a Night assassin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T13:33:45-08:00","id":45817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=45744#post45744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry it's taking me so long. Work's been a bitch lately, and I've spent a shameful amount of time just lying in bed on a heating pad. I'll get something cooked up soon; my biggest stumbling point right now is figuring out a style for this guy. Not, like, a martial arts style, but just a methodology. Since I haven't hear anything from CitanHyuga since this thread started, I might rework my dude to be a Twilight spy rather than a Night assassin.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've heard from CitanHyuga, he's either probably going to be making a Sidereal. If he does make a Twilight, though, they'll most likely be a Crafter-Swordsman, so I doubt that it'll be much of a problem to have two Twilights, if yours is a spy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T13:48:46-08:00","id":45828,"title":"","content":"Jesus. Maybe I should go Sidereal too and we just run a Sidereal game. Is anyone still Lunaring it up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T13:54:39-08:00","id":45832,"title":"","content":"Dietaku's making a Lunar, which he told me is nearly done. Plus, from what I last heard, FallenEco and Horngeek are both making Solars, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T16:12:47-08:00","id":45899,"title":"","content":"Hey Noodle, do you have a particular culture for the setting in mind? I just had a bit of inspiration, but would like a little info from you before I buy it a wedding ring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T16:21:28-08:00","id":45905,"title":"","content":"Vaguely Ancient Hellenic, in the sense that Familial/Clan loyalty is a Very Big Deal, and that they would tend to spend all summer fighting border skirmishes with their neighbors. Romance of the Three Kingdoms era China also springs to mind. What's your idea? Regardless of my ideas, everything is very fluid right now at my end, so chances are I'll be able to work it in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T17:00:17-08:00","id":45916,"title":"","content":"My own sheet will probably be done by... the end of the weekend-ish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T17:05:24-08:00","id":45923,"title":"","content":"That's alright. I'm going to plan on starting the actual game early next week, maybe Monday or Tuesday. Just to give you all a rough &quot;deadline&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T17:25:03-08:00","id":45935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=45832#post45832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dietaku's making a Lunar, which he told me is nearly done. Plus, from what I last heard, FallenEco and Horngeek are both making Solars, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>She's done, and I showed her to you. I'm just transcribing my notes to a word document I can upload. I'm not the fastest at writing, though, and Exalted characters are a lot of info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T17:38:11-08:00","id":45938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=45905#post45905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vaguely Ancient Hellenic, in the sense that Familial/Clan loyalty is a Very Big Deal, and that they would tend to spend all summer fighting border skirmishes with their neighbors. Romance of the Three Kingdoms era China also springs to mind. What's your idea? Regardless of my ideas, everything is very fluid right now at my end, so chances are I'll be able to work it in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, well, I guess it's less an idea than a motif or a visual. One of the things holding me up is how I want to have my own niche, yet the idea of a monk-murderer looking for enlightenment through violence not only heavily implies martial arts, it also suggests a focus on combat that, given how many martial artists we already have, I just don't think we need any more of (though I suppose if I wanted to be a complete prick, I could do it anyway just to lord my Solar dice pools over everyone). I want to play a bad man who suddenly has memories of being a good one; a loner who has memories of a time when his circle was closer to him than brothers born. I want internal conflict, and as much as I like the idea of ripping off Amarant, this just isn't the place for that.<br /> <br /> I asked you for more information because I'm casting about for inspiration. I had a thought about pre-Columbian South American culture (East = wood = jungle = Amazon), but it doesn't sound like you're going that way, and I don't ultimately mind that. It wasn't even an idea, really, as much as a place I could go to books to start reading up for ideas.<br /> <br /> It sounds like filial duty is the angle I need to focus on here. Someone who does bad things because the family tells him to, but now has a perspective that allows him to see the world outside of his family. I just need to think of something to do with that idea. Clan assassin is still possible, but seems trite. I'd like something more interesting. Maybe a character assassin, or spy, or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T18:08:00-08:00","id":45956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=45938#post45938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er, well, I guess it's less an idea than a motif or a visual. One of the things holding me up is how I want to have my own niche, yet the idea of a monk-murderer looking for enlightenment through violence not only heavily implies martial arts, it also suggests a focus on combat that, given how many martial artists we already have, I just don't think we need any more of (though I suppose if I wanted to be a complete prick, I could do it anyway just to lord my Solar dice pools over everyone). I want to play a bad man who suddenly has memories of being a good one; a loner who has memories of a time when his circle was closer to him than brothers born. I want internal conflict, and as much as I like the idea of ripping off Amarant, this just isn't the place for that.<br /> <br /> I asked you for more information because I'm casting about for inspiration. I had a thought about pre-Columbian South American culture (East = wood = jungle = Amazon), but it doesn't sound like you're going that way, and I don't ultimately mind that. It wasn't even an idea, really, as much as a place I could go to books to start reading up for ideas.<br /> <br /> It sounds like filial duty is the angle I need to focus on here. Someone who does bad things because the family tells him to, but now has a perspective that allows him to see the world outside of his family. I just need to think of something to do with that idea. Clan assassin is still possible, but seems trite. I'd like something more interesting. Maybe a character assassin, or spy, or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it may help to understand some more about Noodle's understanding of the area (We're brothers, you see). He sees the Hundred Kingdoms as the Balkans of the Scavenger Lands, and so, the area always seemed somewhat Greek to him. Now, I get where you're coming from, too, in regards to the East being largely about Jungles and all, and, my understanding of Aztec culture is that the two aren't entirely unmarriable. Aztecs had a strong clan affiliation, and also had a lust for war that was a foundation of their society. Heck, having a flamboyant caste of warrior-poets devoted to the City Mother by offering her the spoils of war in terms of goods and slaves would be a compelling and dangerous faction to deal with, considering how Spirit politics intermingle with Human politics in Exalted.<br /> <br /> Thus, you character could be part of a noble house, dedicated to your clan and your way of life, deovted to the City Mother and her imposed culture and government, but, after your exaltation, could realize that, ultimately, the way things are is going to cause the City to spiral into self-destruction. However, this is the only life you know. Plus, now a buncha dick-foreigners are coming in and beginning to mosey in on your turf (I mean both NPC AND PC foreigners, mind). That opens up not only conflict in terms of inter-PC objectives, but also conflict in terms of what your PC knows and what he is comfortable with.<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T18:29:33-08:00","id":45973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=45935#post45935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She's done, and I showed her to you. I'm just transcribing my notes to a word document I can upload. I'm not the fastest at writing, though, and Exalted characters are a lot of info.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what is slowing me down...just not sure I'm happy with my Eclipse. Feels like I'm missing something in his backstory, not sure what...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T19:15:47-08:00","id":45995,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, the Scavenger Lands are culturally very different from the East, even if they are technically part of it. The Hundred Kingdoms are many, small, their power balance always shifting, and have something of a medieval Europe feel to them. <br /> <br /> I don't know if you've read the King's Assassin series... It's probably not necessary... But an assassin loyal to one of these many kingdoms, who preserves it against more powerful opponents not by military strength, but by careful murder, would fit right in. Though it's just an idea. A diplomat-spy would work just as well - Elias is basically this (canon Haslanti Night Caste) and he's pretty cool. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, because of the balkanized nature of the setting, it is very easy for a spy, thief or assassin for hire to wander the Kingdoms under a cover identity (say, minstrel, musician, merchant), getting hired from place to place without anyone ever really figuring out his true job. That assumes little loyalty to a single place, though. <br /> <br /> Going from Greek inspirations... Orpheus as a secret spy as well as a perfect singer, or a wandering strongman like Hercules... None of which would work best as a Night Caste, but I don't remember much famous spies/assassins from Greek myth or history, sadly. <br /> <br /> Sorry, I'm not having great ideas right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T19:46:13-08:00","id":46008,"title":"","content":"I got it! Bounty hunter. Guilt and innocence meant nothing, only the paycheck at the end of the hunt did; and now he's a Lawgiver with an uncomfortable sense that he's supposed to care about more than liquid cash.<br /> <br /> I should have a sheet ready sometime late tomorrow (seriously, work is kicking my ass).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T20:28:33-08:00","id":46021,"title":"","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> I have been extremely busy and have had so much chaos going on with the group I have been STing, work, and the testing, but I now have everything taken care of. Sorry I have not gotten back to the thread in a while. I am planning on playing a Twilight Crafter/Swordsman. His name is Hyuga.<br /> <br /> He pretends to be gruff, but is secretly a kind person that really just wants to be a friend to everyone. He can't help but try to look cool and in control the whole time. He was born in paragon and sought to get out of the busy life of traders. He just wants to do his thing crafting and making friends. He has no real interest in making money, building alliances, or settling down.<br /> <br /> His father had been a blacksmith and he sought to be like him since he was a wee lad. Sadly, his father died when he was eight years old. His mother raised him after his father's death until she finally died of overwork shortly after he turned 15. At this time he sought a job and was brought in by a friend of his dad, a master blacksmith in the city. Working for this gruff man, he picked up his habits quickly, but never forgot the loving care of his parents. He worked for the artisan and showed plenty of aptitude for the job. He even picked up Riverspeak from all of the travelling guildsmen and traders. After he turned 25, he quickly became a strong artisan himself. He eventually created many works of steel that impressed even his new guardian, Loheim. After Loheim had taught him all he knew, he sent Hyuga off to explore and get new ideas for crafting throughout creation. Hyuga became a nomad searching for inspiration for new works of art in the east. He traveled around until he was 32. He learned to craft even without the best of tools and started to appreciate the art of his objects even more.<br /> <br /> Finally, he came across a town in distress. They were consistently pillaged and burned down by the surrounding beast-man tribes. After hearing about several people losing fathers, mothers, sisters, brothers, and more, he brought it upon himself to help these people with the only skill he knew: Blacksmithing. He forged many weapons for the villagers to defend themselves with. He became great friends with the villagers and stayed for many moons. Shortly after he headed out of the village, he heard the shouts and screams of friends and the other villagers. He knew the beast-men must have come back. He ran back into the village. He saw many of them falling in battle, unable to use his weapons properly and being outmatched by the beast-men. He swiftly grabbed a sword of the ground. It was then that he realized that he had never learned how to use these tools. He knew that he could never be a true artisan like this and could not help protect anyone as he was, but he was damn well going to try his best.<br /> <br /> After fighting a few beast-men, he came to the middle of the city to see an anathema *a Solar* killing his closest friend, Chloe Mist, whilst laughing. Enraged he leaped at the anathema's back with his sword, but it was deftly broken and knocked away with complete ease. He rushed the Solar trying to knock him down and was swiftly knocked to the ground with a leaping kick. Stunned and very hurt, he watched through teary eyes as the Solar taunted him saying, &quot;You have a problem puny man?&quot; The Solar then grabbed his friend's mother by the neck and turned towards Hyuga. Once again enraged and full of adrenaline, he got up and ran at the Solar eyeing the orichalcum sword on his belt. He rushed in and managed to duck under the swift fist that Solar threw at him and dove at the sword. With all his might he tried to take and raise the sword, but it was impossible for him. The Solar then grabbed him by the neck and said, &quot;Say goodbye to your friend,&quot; while making him face his friend's mother. With tears in his eyes he struggled and managed to kick the sword causing it to put a gash in the Solar's arm, that was carrying the woman; a complete miracle. He then felt he had solved some sort of riddle of artifact weaponry in his head. It was then that time seemed to stand still as the glory of the Unconquered Sun came upon him whilst hearing, &quot;Use my power and knowledge well. Do not tarnish my gift. I expect many things of you.&quot; With his new caste mark and anima shining brightly, he escaped the confused and slightly blinded Solar's grip and dove for a sword and swung it deftly at his chest causing a great amount of blood to spurt upon the ground. The Solar in great amount of pain and fear, retreated quickly whilst dropping his sword. Hyuga was left there; an anathema for all the village to see. He had become something he had never believed he would... or could... he did not know what to do or how the town would react. He quickly picked up the orichalcum sword and darted from the town, never to return. He has not looked back at the town ever since....<br /> <br /> This character is partially inspired by Cid from the Final Fantasy series. I will send in all his info soon. I can find a picture of him now.<br /> <br /> Also, I do have the game I ST on Tuesdays, so my posting may slow down a bit then. I cannot wait to see everyone's finished characters.<br /> <br /> Edit: I have uploaded a \u200bpicture of how I imagine him as my avatar. Just imagine his skin being a bit darker. And a bit older than he looks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","user":"CitanHyuga","date":". 01-10-2014, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T20:43:23-08:00","id":46031,"title":"","content":"Noodle, would you say that Investigation or Survival is more appropriate for tracking rolls? Would both apply?<br /> <br /> Is there a Deathlord nearby you intend to use that you can name without spoiling anything? I'm considering the possibility of having an Abyssal Mentor to justify sorcery, assuming I don't decide sorcery is stupid and just forget about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T21:15:31-08:00","id":46045,"title":"","content":"I would say that both Investigation and Survival are applicable. I don't have a particular Deathlord in mind at the moment, but I was most likely going to make one. So if you want to make up a name for one, I'll run with it. Though I would think a divine, lunar, or sidereal Sorcery mentor would probably be easier to justify, in character. Just a thought<br /> <br /> Looking at it there appears to be a communication error, which was entirely my fault. When I said vaguely Hellenic, I meant along the lines of:<br /> <br /> (1) The political climate is similar to Pre-Persian Wars Hellas. There are many poloi, which are culturally similar, but are constantly at low-level warfare with each other. Alliances are short-lived at best, and are full of treachery. Should one polis get significantly stronger than the others, nearby poloi will team up to put the smack down on them. <br /> (2) Each polis is comprised of a handful of Clans/Tribes/Gentes which collectively contain all Citizens. These familial groupings are the true political power in the polis. The actual government is more akin to a confederation which represents the collective Clans/Tribes/Gentes to the other poloi. Duty to your family is equivalent (and in many cases synonymous with) duty to your nation.<br /> <br /> That was really all I meant. Even here, I'm just saying Poloi because I don't want to have to keep typing out city-state all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T21:28:44-08:00","id":46051,"title":"","content":"I was thinking Abyssal mentor for two reasons. The first is that my guy (thinking of calling him Saramandu, though I'm pretty sure that's just a collection of nonsense syllables) spent his mortal life as someone who killed when it profited him, and that would make him interesting to Abyssals as a potential convert. The other is that I want memories of First Age camaraderie to be a big part of his story, and if his mentor is secretly one of his old circlemates, that could set up interesting conflict as well as justify why the two of them have a connection to each other.<br /> <br /> I'm not married to the idea, though. Like I said, I'm not even totally sure I want to bother with sorcery. I'm just explaining my thought process to you while I keep thinking about where to put dots on paper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T05:23:18-08:00","id":46185,"title":"","content":"I don't regret my decision to go Archery for main combat tactic--we need ranged support, and it also fits the concept of a dude who wants to profit from combat, not take risks letting them kill him--but all you Sidereals make me jealous of how much more fun your Archery Charms are than Solar ones. More quixotic, maybe, but more fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T07:05:36-08:00","id":46880,"title":"","content":"Guys, and particularly Omicron, I'm sorry, but I think I have to withdraw my bid to play. I just seem incapable of getting an idea I can execute. I have plenty of ideas, and plenty of executions, but none of them are ever for the same character; like, my latest idea, the bounty hunter I've been talking about, I can't for my life think of anything to fill in for Motivation or Intimacies (I think this is because the idea of existential self-doubt is fundamentally flawed as a character concept for a game like Exalted where the mechanics demand the character be self-assured and driven rather than conflicted).<br /> <br /> My thanks to everyone who was willing to put up with me to this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T10:16:26-08:00","id":46958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=46880#post46880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, and particularly Omicron, I'm sorry, but I think I have to withdraw my bid to play. I just seem incapable of getting an idea I can execute. I have plenty of ideas, and plenty of executions, but none of them are ever for the same character; like, my latest idea, the bounty hunter I've been talking about, I can't for my life think of anything to fill in for Motivation or Intimacies (I think this is because the idea of existential self-doubt is fundamentally flawed as a character concept for a game like Exalted where the mechanics demand the character be self-assured and driven rather than conflicted).<br /> <br /> My thanks to everyone who was willing to put up with me to this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to see you go, Jim. You're welcome back anytime, if you can get a character you're content with off the ground. I encourage you to check in on the IC and OOC threads every so often; something in there might inspire you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T11:29:39-08:00","id":46991,"title":"","content":"Aaaaw.<br /> <br /> For that matter, I really liked the concept of Jagger, and would have quite enjoyed seeing him in play. Maybe you could join in later if you have a burst of inspiration from how the actual game proceeds? <br /> <br /> I wish I had more susbtantial help to provide, but you seem to have been sifting through character concepts a lot, so sitting down and trying to define one more clearly can't work if you don't have a good basis on which one to work on in the first place.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly sorry to see you go u_u","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T21:03:38-08:00","id":47236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=46991#post46991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly sorry to see you go u_u</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. I've wanted to play with you for ages. I just don't seem to have any good material in me at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T06:41:53-08:00","id":47355,"title":"","content":"I woke up from a dream this morning with an idea for a Sidereal matchmaker whose sacrifice to learn sorcery was that she could never have for herself what her duty to Creation compelled her to create for others.<br /> <br /> I can't really pull that specific idea into this game when we already have a Joybringer, but I will think about the &quot;sacrifice to learn sorcery was that she could never have for herself what her duty to Creation compelled her to create for others&quot; bit because I bet I could make a good character concept out of that conflict. I'll noodle it around today. My immediate reaction is to think about Zenith ideas, because suffering for your beliefs is definitely a Zenith thing, but what to do with it...<br /> <br /> Suggestions welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T09:16:28-08:00","id":47424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=47355#post47355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I woke up from a dream this morning with an idea for a Sidereal matchmaker whose sacrifice to learn sorcery was that she could never have for herself what her duty to Creation compelled her to create for others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Amelie of Montmatre as an Exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T09:58:17-08:00","id":47444,"title":"","content":"The simplest way I can see to do this is to pull a complete reversal and go Battles. The person I'm imagining is akin to the Chosen of Battles as Iron Siaka is to the Serenity's. Viewed as something of an eccentric, because they use their knowledge of Serenity/Battles to know when to remove it. Instead of your sacrifice being that you'll never know your purview, it could be that you'll never know respite from it. That would have a very similar effect, while still keeping the core concept (from what you said) intact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T10:11:45-08:00","id":47447,"title":"","content":"I personally do not see why we cannot have more than one member that is a &quot;joybringer.&quot; I think it gives even more reason for those members to gather. A sidereal sorcerer would also be very interesting to see.<br /> <br /> Another concept I was toying with that you might like is a Zenith caste that was once a gladiator. He was simply a slave that was put into the gladiator ring one day and has fought for his life since then, He fought countless battles gaining immense fighting skills and learned to appeal to any crowd. Eventually, an anathema joined a fight in the coliseum. After seeing his friends, well known combatants, and other individuals get mowed down by this anathema easily without even showing of their true capabilities, he realized how fragile life is and that every person does truly have a gift. He gathered together the remaining combatants with his mere presence and fame and used their skills (even non-combatant skills) to bring down the anathema. Their effort seemed to be almost for naught until he decided to pray. He did not know why or who he was praying to, but he wanted to stop the rest of the combatants being killed without even any dignity or honor. He then thought that no gods were listening and thought that he himself must be the one to show everyone that this treatment of slaves and talented individuals should not be treated as toys and entertainment. He decided to use his great combat prowess to show it. He rushed the anathema and the rest followed suit. Eventually, they managed to knockout the anathema and the whole crowed cheered wanting to see him killed. Just then he called out to the crowd and spoke his mind about slavery, honor, and killing. As he continued to speak, the Unconquered Sun bestowed upon him his exaltation as a Zenith. He realized then that his prayer had been answered as the crowd listened in awe to his beliefs. Now, he wants to end slavery and wants everyone to see the power and caring of the Unconquered Sun. He goes around to many temples praying in thanks and tries to bring out the true skills of those that he meets. <br /> <br /> Feel free to adapt or change anything you want about him if you are interested in it. I have him stated as a priest warrior, but you can do whatever you like. His favored abilities for me were athletics, melee, awareness, dodge, and socialize. I also put some into war and medicine. His attributes were phys/social/mental. Again, feel free to change anything if you are interested.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T10:58:22-08:00","id":47481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=47444#post47444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The simplest way I can see to do this is to pull a complete reversal and go Battles.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea. I'm only considering Solars right now because I wanted to work with Omicron that way, but the idea of a Solar general whose goal is peace but who knows he can only achieve it through war...I like that idea.<br /> <br /> Shame I hate mass combat, though. Maybe I need to go back to the assassin thing, someone whose job is to serve the law but never know the peace of it, or something like that but less crappy. I don't know, a killer whose job is to cleanse the world of evil at the cost of defiling his own karma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=47447#post47447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally do not see why we cannot have more than one member that is a &quot;Joybringer.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I dislike doubling up on another player's caste. It makes me feel rude, because while character personalities and approaches will always differ, there's a certain amount of inevitable stepping on toes and inviting competition between characters and even players as to who is the best at what they both do. I'd just rather not do that to someone who had a bunch of character ideas and settled on the one he did because he likes it best; remind me to tell you some time how much I hated the last year or two of my previous Exalted game when some dude pulled that crap on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T11:19:36-08:00","id":47496,"title":"","content":"Hey, if Sidereal works better for you, don't sweat it; there can be another Solar, or Sea can be looking for a Solar rather than currently working with them. As long as the PCs have any Solar members at all, it works out for me.<br /> <br /> Sea of Tears is a weird Joybringer; she doesn't partake of most of the pleasures she brings to others. I would have asked for something like the Oathbound Flaw (an Oath relating to chastity or ascetism, to represent her &quot;bet&quot;) if that didn't make me feel like a cheat because I'm wary of Flaws and Merits. A Serenity who actually enjoys the benefits of her Caste could be a very interesting foil, and if you focus on Sorcery and I on Martial Arts we probably wouldn't be stepping on each other's toes. Still, the idea of the Battles answer to Iron Siaka's Serenity is interesting.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, a Zenith Sorcerer with that idea... Hm. Mortal thaumaturge/shaman/exorcist who spent most of their life negociating with and banishing evil spirits, and considered their Exaltation the bestowal of a greater responsibility - and such obtained Sorcery through their dedication to the protection of Creation at the cost of personal comfort and happiness in a normal life. Possibly, as a mortal, cursed by one of the spirits they banished to never know love, a curse which was scoured away by their Exaltation - without changing much, as they now consider that such affairs would distract them from a greater duty. A decision to never settle, to always found a new place to save or protect.<br /> <br /> Not sure if that's the kind of idea you were looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 01-12-2014, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T05:29:13-08:00","id":48086,"title":"","content":"Random note apropos of almost nothing: I cannot help that pretty much all of my ideas lately are for criminals and murderers. I also cannot help noting none of my ideas really work.<br /> <br /> Causation is not proven, but correlation is suggested.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should just go with a nice guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 01-13-2014, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T16:39:23-08:00","id":48575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=48086#post48086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random note apropos of almost nothing: I cannot help that pretty much all of my ideas lately are for criminals and murderers. I also cannot help noting none of my ideas really work.<br /> <br /> Causation is not proven, but correlation is suggested.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should just go with a nice guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, you're so nice, you loop around to being a complete hard-ass. I actually had considered running a Solar in this vein, a man who so loved his adoptive father that when he accidentally killed him, he became something of a monster, jaded by the event. I was going to model this with high compassion and conviction, with high fighting ability, becoming the kind of monster he was trained to defeat initially. Feel free to steal from this, 'cuz I sure did. The link below may help illuminate how.<br /> <a href=\"http://hokuto.wikia.com/wiki/Souther\" target=\"_blank\">http://hokuto.wikia.com/wiki/Souther</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T18:48:38-08:00","id":48640,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm thinking...I don't know if there's a specific term for what I'm thinking. I'd call him a social worker in our day and world; someone who works with children who are at risk in society. Someone who runs an orphanage, maybe an official one but more likely someone who takes in strays and tries to help them grow up right. I'm not sure how I can leverage that into a sacrifice for sorcery, though. I mean, I know I want his sacrifice to be that he will only be a caregiver, but will never have a child of his own, but I am having a hard time contriving circumstances whereby to learn sorcery, he has to lose his daddy factory. I may need to think of a more metaphorical sacrifice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T11:05:39-08:00","id":49139,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, was able to use the Internet Wayback Machine to dig up Holden's old Wind-Cutting Blade Style. Not sure if the person who was looking for it moved on to other things, but anyway. Link: <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20120725121427/http://wiki.white-wolf.com/exalted/index.php?title=Wind-Cutting_Blade_Style\" target=\"_blank\">http://web.archive.org/web/201207251...ng_Blade_Style</a><br /> <br /> Since I come bearing gifts, I wonder if there's room for one more person in here? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1994-stillwinds","name":"StillWinds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T11:40:01-08:00","id":49168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StillWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=49139#post49139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, was able to use the Internet Wayback Machine to dig up Holden's old Wind-Cutting Blade Style. Not sure if the person who was looking for it moved on to other things, but anyway. Link: <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20120725121427/http://wiki.white-wolf.com/exalted/index.php?title=Wind-Cutting_Blade_Style\" target=\"_blank\">http://web.archive.org/web/201207251...ng_Blade_Style</a><br /> <br /> Since I come bearing gifts, I wonder if there's room for one more person in here? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, is this an actually functional archive of the Wiki? It IS! Well, kind of... Huh. I'm going to have to plumb through this, and see what Awesomeness I can salvage. <br /> <br /> I believe Other Things Were Moved On To in regard to the style, but thanks. This is a HUGE help to me, since now know how to potentially access large portions of lost homebrew. Now I just have to put the work into digging it all out. <br /> <br /> Since you come bearing gifts, I will allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T20:50:32-08:00","id":49519,"title":"","content":"My Lunar is up and ready. Also, welcome to the newcomer! I hope we all have fun together!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T21:25:40-08:00","id":49551,"title":"","content":"This is really weird... the forum seems to randomly update for me. Sometimes I see posts then nothing for a while. I will come back a few minutes later to re-read something and suddenly like 20 posts are there &gt;&gt; <br /> <br /> @JimB &quot;Random note apropos of almost nothing: I cannot help that pretty much all of my ideas lately are for criminals and murderers.&quot;<br /> I just thought about that. You could always be a con-man that helps give advice on how to not be conned (even if it is to the highest bidders). He could be helpful even though he is a criminal. A character like that could probably smell a trap or con a mile away and be able to help the entire group.<br /> <br /> I do love the idea of someone with an orphanage though. (Can you say ward dots?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T23:00:29-08:00","id":49578,"title":"","content":"*looks at Dietaku's sheet, fails a Temperance roll*<br /> <br /> ...so, hm, mind if I take a couple Flaws as well? &gt;.&gt; Stuff that I intended to roleplay anyway...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:28:27-08:00","id":49940,"title":"","content":"Omicron- Sure. I said Merits and Flaws were allowed. <br /> <br /> As you may have noticed, my intended start-time of Monday or Tuesday this week didn't pan out. However, since we now have three finished characters, I will be starting the game on this upcoming Sunday. If your character is not up by then, that's cool, and I'll work them into the game once you finish them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:50:03-08:00","id":49951,"title":"","content":"Two questions: can I start the game with Ascendent/Resplendent Destinies? If so, how many, and how should I handle the rolls? <br /> <br /> Additionally, would you be open to allowing <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\">these Sidereal Charms?</a> I'm specifically interested in the Presence, Performance and Integrity Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T12:25:57-08:00","id":49970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=49578#post49578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*looks at Dietaku's sheet, fails a Temperance roll*<br /> <br /> ...so, hm, mind if I take a couple Flaws as well? &gt;.&gt; Stuff that I intended to roleplay anyway...</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://s11.postimg.org/6x9rbvv43/sample_cb8b276efe6dde53d3c261d835af904b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I guess I did something right, then, if Tirien is causing people to fail Temperance, although I probably would avoid her if she was someone I'd meet. I see her as being pretty much a THAT GIRL; proud, vain, and unwilling to compromise due to her highborn status. <br /> <br /> If anyone needs any ideas or anything, though, I'm open to assist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T12:38:09-08:00","id":49983,"title":"","content":"Great! Looking forward to this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My idea is Ragara Malakai, a Dawn Caste child of a Dynastic house who was brought up in the Realm thinking he would Exalt as a Dragon-Blooded, and then through some trick of heritage never did. Finally he joined the Wild Hunt as a mortal patrician soldier, and Exalted Solar while his unit was bringing down an Abyssal in the Threshold. Of course he immediately had to kill all of his former colleagues, so now he's struggling with his new status as an Anathema pushing against his love for the Realm and his inability to ever go back.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, he fights using a jade daiklave (for now, hopefully there's an orichalcum one in his future!) and a combination of Solar Melee and Five-Dragon Style, which he learned as a mortal in the Realm's primary school system. He also makes use of Swallowing the Lotus Root to get XP breaks on his TMA charms. Out of combat, he's moderately persuasive, but quite gifted at calligraphy.<br /> <br /> How's that sound? If it works I'll have a sheet up in the OOC thread by tonight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1994-stillwinds","name":"StillWinds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T13:11:30-08:00","id":50015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StillWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=49983#post49983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great! Looking forward to this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My idea is Ragara Malakai, a Dawn Caste child of a Dynastic house who was brought up in the Realm thinking he would Exalt as a Dragon-Blooded, and then through some trick of heritage never did. Finally he joined the Wild Hunt as a mortal patrician soldier, and Exalted Solar while his unit was bringing down an Abyssal in the Threshold. Of course he immediately had to kill all of his former colleagues, so now he's struggling with his new status as an Anathema pushing against his love for the Realm and his inability to ever go back.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, he fights using a jade daiklave (for now, hopefully there's an orichalcum one in his future!) and a combination of Solar Melee and Five-Dragon Style, which he learned as a mortal in the Realm's primary school system. He also makes use of Swallowing the Lotus Root to get XP breaks on his TMA charms. Out of combat, he's moderately persuasive, but quite gifted at calligraphy.<br /> <br /> How's that sound? If it works I'll have a sheet up in the OOC thread by tonight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually pretty eerie, considering that's more or less Tirien's back-story, her full name being Ledaal Tirien, although Malakai seems going with his lack of Exaltation better than Tirien did. This could work well, though, as Noodle and I made up a Genealogy for Tirien, and her father married into the Ledaals from House Ragara. Mayhaps we could be cousins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T13:58:32-08:00","id":50052,"title":"","content":"Oh man, totally missed that in the lead-in. I don't want to step on any backstory-related toes here, but on the other hand it could be interesting to have someone who's going through a lot of the same stuff as Malakai. I kind of had him pegged not really as a guaranteed-to-Exalt golden boy - more a child of an outlier branch member of Ragara and some mortal patrician in the hopes that they'd get lucky. His lack of breeding ultimately doomed him to failure in his quest for the Breath of the Dragons, but his natural talent with the sword caused the Unconquered Sun to rectify the mistake.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'm happy switching up backstories if you feel it's too similar to yours. The character would remain unchanged - maybe a simple mortal orphan from Arjuf who was taken in by a dojo and trained that way. Let me know what you want to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1994-stillwinds","name":"StillWinds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T14:07:53-08:00","id":50058,"title":"","content":"@Stillwinds: Not at all. I think it makes for an interesting synergy between us,especially considering how well that it all ties together. I actually had some plans for Tirien to remain in contact with some of her Ragara cousins in Greyfalls so as to present a respectable front for her efforts to take over the city, namely using her social charms to create demand for the ever-popular, easy and cheap to make &quot;Meat on a Stick, Now with Turnips and Mustard,&quot; and then to put all her revenue into a Ragara-backed account (She has to keep her funds inside the Family, after all). <br /> <br /> So, in essence, go ahead with your initial idea. I wasn't angry or anything, just offering a potential character connection between us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T14:09:05-08:00","id":50060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=49951#post49951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions: can I start the game with Ascendent/Resplendent Destinies? If so, how many, and how should I handle the rolls?<br /> <br /> Additionally, would you be open to allowing <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\">these Sidereal Charms?</a> I'm specifically interested in the Presence, Performance and Integrity Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding Ascendant/Resplendent destinies. You can start the game with them, go ahead and make the rolls yourself; I trust you to not fudge the dice.<br /> Regarding the Other charms. They look well-built, so I'll okay them, tentatively. I'm going to look in more depth in a bit, but unless I say they're not okay, continue with the assumption that they are. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StillWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=49983#post49983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great! Looking forward to this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My idea is Ragara Malakai, a Dawn Caste child of a Dynastic house who was brought up in the Realm thinking he would Exalt as a Dragon-Blooded, and then through some trick of heritage never did. Finally he joined the Wild Hunt as a mortal patrician soldier, and Exalted Solar while his unit was bringing down an Abyssal in the Threshold. Of course he immediately had to kill all of his former colleagues, so now he's struggling with his new status as an Anathema pushing against his love for the Realm and his inability to ever go back.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, he fights using a jade daiklave (for now, hopefully there's an orichalcum one in his future!) and a combination of Solar Melee and Five-Dragon Style, which he learned as a mortal in the Realm's primary school system. He also makes use of Swallowing the Lotus Root to get XP breaks on his TMA charms. Out of combat, he's moderately persuasive, but quite gifted at calligraphy.<br /> <br /> How's that sound? If it works I'll have a sheet up in the OOC thread by tonight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds good, if a bit similar to Dietaku's. Mechanically, I once did something similar, with a Sidereal that went into Violet Bier of Sorrows and Five-Dragon. After a bit I realized that, for all of the thematic goodness of going into FDS, it was rather underwhelming for a Celestial-level exalt. And that was with me juggling two charm-trees of the same ability. Even with the Swallowing the Lotus Root, it'll be expensive for you to juggle MA and Melee. Not saying that you can't do it, but I'm advising you to think about it before you commit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T14:21:35-08:00","id":50070,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Do you have a preferred online dice roller? I tend to use invisiblecastle because I can link directly to the result. Should I post the results of my rolls here, or in the OOC thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T14:36:40-08:00","id":50087,"title":"","content":"I've allowed my players to use whatever sort of dice-roller they want in the past, be it an online Dice roller, dicetools, or actual physical dice. That said, all the PbP games I've ran have been on a very small, pretty amicable forum, so there was a gentleman's agreement of sorts that you would be honest with your rolls. I'm personally inclined to follow that, but I recognize that part of what made that system functional is that we were a very small, tight community. My concern would be that if someone got a sequence of really good rolls, another player might think that they're fudging the dice.<br /> <br /> In order to prevent that from happening, I'm inclined to say invisiblecastle or something else that lets you prove your rolls (I had no idea such a thing existed, but I'm not really surprised). If y'all don't think it will be a problem, then I would say to not worry about it and use whatever you feel comfortable with.<br /> <br /> The rolls for the destinies should be posted in the OOC thread, by editing either your charsheet, the post it's in, or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":".  altered wording to clarify meaning 01-15-2014, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:39:15-08:00","id":50169,"title":"","content":"Suddenly I really miss the Simple Astrology rules from Shards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T16:59:32-08:00","id":50242,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but I am not happy with the work on Willow I've done.<br /> I am going to drop out, rather than hold you all up because I'm fussing over my character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T17:50:24-08:00","id":50285,"title":"","content":"You're not using Shards hacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T17:53:55-08:00","id":50289,"title":"","content":"Sorry to see you go, Eco.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=50285#post50285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not using Shards hacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not for astrology. While the system is simpler, it doesn't come anywhere near the potency of standard Manual:Fate-Ninjas Astrology. Which, while it takes a long while to master is TOTALLY worth it once you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T18:52:00-08:00","id":50328,"title":"","content":"Hey Omicron, what do you think of being the mentor/guiding hand to a former priest of an ancestor cult whose faith was shattered by the visions of his Exaltation because he'd always believed that the ancestors watch over us throughout our lives from a holy and transcendent afterlife and that ghosts are those who have chosen to stay behind to assist the living, only to find out from his Exaltation that death is the end and ghosts are nothing more than damned half-souls with no more power than what they can grab from magic tricks? A guy who was so wounded by this information he can't even bring himself to have faith in the Unconquered Sun despite the miracle of being Exalted by him, because who knows, maybe the Unconquered Sun is just some freak with magic tricks and his own agenda? A guy who can't bring himself to tell the truth to his former congregation because he can't bear to inflict on them the same damage that was done to him, and is trying to not only guide his flock gently into a new direction (which will probably mean lying to them about revelations to subtly change the dogma) but also to find purpose in his life again and reconcile the idea that he's to rule in the name of a god he has no wonder or love for?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Perhaps a deliberate choice to bear the weight of his broken faith and to never reveal the truth to his parishoners is the sacrifice made for his sorcery. I kind of want to take him into necromancy, but fucking necromancy, man...<br /> <br /> EDIT EDIT: I am imagining Sea trying to inspire faith in my guy (I kind of want to call him Sky Blue and Black) by artfully picking ways to describe Heaven so it doesn't sound like her pain-in-the-ass job, where most of her coworkers are at least mildly corrupt and almost every last one of them is a complete dick. That interaction would be funny to me, though I don't know if you think it sounds like a good time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","user":"JimB","date":". 01-15-2014, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T23:54:39-08:00","id":50489,"title":"","content":"I say that it sounds pretty cool and I'm all for it. Their relationship might involve long talks about the process of reincarnation and how death is not truly the end - or is it? And, yes, description of Heaven that, while not lies, might occult part of... or even the majority of... the truth. There is an amusing parallel between Sea's decision to bring the traditional gifts of the House of Serenity to others while she cannot enjoy them herself, and this Solar's decision to pretend for the sake of his followers to believe in something he does not. <br /> <br /> Re: necromancy; some of the tools of necromancy can be found in thaumaturgy, which when bought procedure-by-procedure is actually rather cheap; if you're only after the ability to summon ghosts or exorcise/ward them, it can replace necromancy fairly effectively, and has a few tricks of its own - funeral rites, zombies, nephwracks and whatnot. <br /> <br /> Now you grab that character concept and you <i>don't let it go</i>. I can offer my mechanical expertise in case it's needed, hough I do have a serious problem with optimization, which is that I try to optimize. All the time. I can't help it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T04:00:38-08:00","id":50574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=50489#post50489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you grab that character concept and you <i>don't let it go</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I plan to get a sheet done at work today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T16:27:28-08:00","id":52840,"title":"","content":"So, what's up, everyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T16:49:37-08:00","id":52852,"title":"","content":"My character concept is shallow to the degree that I can't even think of any Favored Abilities to give him, but I don't know how to flesh it out. I am therefore trying to think of what his First Age incarnation was like so I can draw from that to fill in the gaps.<br /> <br /> What's up with you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T18:09:14-08:00","id":52895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=52852#post52852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My character concept is shallow to the degree that I can't even think of any Favored Abilities to give him, but I don't know how to flesh it out. I am therefore trying to think of what his First Age incarnation was like so I can draw from that to fill in the gaps.<br /> <br /> What's up with you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what combat ability will you favor? Melee? To make use of your necromantic sickles, knives and the like? Will your Solar be one of the original Necromancers who plied into the Labyrinth and tore off the sarcophagi of the Neverborn? I think that would be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T18:20:03-08:00","id":52901,"title":"","content":"I looked at it, and really, necromancy does so very little of what I want to do with it that it isn't worth spending my points/Charm selection on. I'd rather wait for Celestial Circle Sorcery to be able to summon a ghost.<br /> <br /> As for a combat Ability...meh. Sky was not a fighter, and giving him combat abilities isn't really in keeping with his character. That's why I'm thinking of his former incarnation. I picture his last self as some kind of hermit-monk-ascetic type who created a philosophy-religion Sky can't really remember but is cynically sure was a lie like all other religions. That lends itself to Martial Arts, but that bores me, so I'm thinking of zen Archery instead; Sky has a fragment of a memory of someone asking him (or his old self), &quot;What is truth?&quot; and his old self answering by picking up a bow and firing a shot into a target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T21:13:08-08:00","id":52981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=52901#post52901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a combat Ability...meh. Sky was not a fighter, and giving him combat abilities isn't really in keeping with his character. That's why I'm thinking of his former incarnation. I picture his last self as some kind of hermit-monk-ascetic type who created a philosophy-religion Sky can't really remember but is cynically sure was a lie like all other religions. That lends itself to Martial Arts, but that bores me, so I'm thinking of zen Archery instead; Sky has a fragment of a memory of someone asking him (or his old self), &quot;What is truth?&quot; and his old self answering by picking up a bow and firing a shot into a target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many temple dwellers were known in Japan to be archers. Many were said to exercise spirits with them. I know your character would depend on ghosts rather than exercising spirits, but it would really fit. I think it would be awesome to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T21:19:14-08:00","id":52985,"title":"","content":"Really? I've seen a few references to magic arrows or sacred arrows or something, but I didn't know there's a social and historical weight behind them. Can you tell me more about it, so I can go look it up myself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T10:21:19-08:00","id":53286,"title":"","content":"<b>Japanese Archery (Kyudo): (the Kyudo is a specific type of bow)</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;In the Nara (710-794) and Heian (794-1185) periods they were utilized in rituals dedicated to the gods; it was around this time that archery made its appearance in events held at the Imperial court.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#505050\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">It is now still practiced, but it began merely as a way to hunt. It was later dedicated to the gods. Also, many temples still hold archery competitions (though not spiritual in nature most of the time). If you look at some mangas that appear around temples, that is where they add the spirituality and magic/sacred arrows which has to do with the exorcism I talked about earlier. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.kyudosocal.com/aboutkyudo.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.kyudosocal.com/aboutkyudo.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.kyudosocal.com/aboutkyudo.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.kyudosocal.com/aboutkyudo.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> This link talks a bit about the meditation that many archery students go through to help with their archery (practicing breathing, etc.). <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Since the beginning of the study of archery in Japan, there has always been a spiritual aspect attributed to the use of the bow and arrow: either to scare away evil spirits or purify space. These spiritual elements of archery are preserved today in kyudo through traditional ritual movements and practices.&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T11:10:32-08:00","id":53322,"title":"","content":"Thanks, CitanHyuga! I got crap going on today, but I'll look this stuff up later tonight when I get back home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T16:20:04-08:00","id":54305,"title":"","content":"Hey, y'all: the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\">IC Thread</a> has been posted! Everyone who hasn't posted a character yet: I'll work you in as soon as you get you guys posted. In the meantime, can anyone who is still working on their characters give me a status update (this is primarily for me to know you're still interested). Also, I posted some things in the OOC thread. You should probably check 'em out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T09:12:28-08:00","id":54708,"title":"","content":"How goes character creation for the rest of you? Anything any of you need help with? I would be glad to try to help with what I can so you can get your character done quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T13:30:58-08:00","id":54863,"title":"","content":"Don't suppose there's still room for more here?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Derp, no, figures that I don't notice that this forum has a PBP forum until it's far too late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2067-alectai","name":"Alectai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T11:49:55-08:00","id":73283,"title":"","content":"*redacted*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","user":"Noodle","date":". 05-07-2014, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T12:48:03-08:00","id":73314,"title":"","content":"Hello Noodle I am interested","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T17:22:30-08:00","id":73461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=73314#post73314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello Noodle I am interested</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat! Well, post your character in the OOC thread once you have them done, and I'll work them once I get an opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T09:04:20-08:00","id":74297,"title":"","content":"Posting immediately in the interest of snagging an open slot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T09:24:03-08:00","id":74308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=74297#post74297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Posting immediately in the interest of snagging an open slot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Congratulations, you got it! For your character, same deal as what I said to Magnusar. And if you want to run ideas by me you can do so here, or in the OOC thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T15:06:31-08:00","id":74585,"title":"","content":"So I have a pretty good idea of what type of character I'm making, I want to know do you allow custom artifact ? I have one that I worked on its not finish and it will require some tweaking but I would like to give it to this character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T15:10:51-08:00","id":74587,"title":"","content":"Sure. What do you have in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T15:20:18-08:00","id":74594,"title":"","content":"Well this character will fight using glorious solar saber so this artifact is basically a daiklave handle without a blade that focus the glorious solar saber into it giving it incredible abilities it is very specific as it focus the charm into a daiklave whatever the type of weapon you would normally produce with it. It is a level 5 artifact so I don't know if you allow people to start with things like this. Some of its powers include that it acts as ssence lens for the damage and double the mote you gain for you're overdrive pool I thought about things like adding to you're PDV and making you're attack Unblockable but it seems a bit boring or not enough I'm not sure like I said its not finished yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 02-18-2014, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T20:38:29-08:00","id":74753,"title":"","content":"I noticed that there is both a Lunar ruler-to-be and a Twilight crafter. I fear that competence in either of those areas would be an asset or a problem?<br /> <br /> My first pass at a character concept was an ex Sorcerer-Engineer from Lookshy who was forced to flee the area after Exalting. As a craftsman he would focus more on manses and infrastructure than Hyuga seems to be and is less interested in personal rulership than Ledaal Tirien. Still, it seems a dangerously thin line to walk. Would a conquering general/former Gunzosha be more suitable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-18-2014, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T20:47:59-08:00","id":74757,"title":"","content":"Exthalion are you going with dawn caste ? I was going for that but you can have it if you want it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T20:50:08-08:00","id":74758,"title":"","content":"Feel free to take it. I was just suggested it as a way to distance myself mechanically from the current players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T20:53:54-08:00","id":74760,"title":"","content":"thanks I feel more comfortable with a dawn but you might try a Zenith, it might be useful the whole strength through unity and unity through faith is a killer in exalted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T20:56:08-08:00","id":74763,"title":"","content":"That is my current plan. However, Ledaal Tirien is a Lunar with a lot of social skill and the motivation of building a new Realm. Too much Zenith would risk overwhelming that with my own vision.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though I suppose there could be some synergy in their goals.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: I noticed by Hyuga's sheet that we seem to be going with the core crafting rules. While by no means a deal breaker, I would like to request that you consider the common houserule that Craft is all one ability. Much like Performance or Linguistics, the diversity of the ability is no indication of the split and the 8-12 Craft skills is an XP tax on crafters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-19-2014, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T10:54:35-08:00","id":75066,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with having a Zenith, or even your Twilight idea, Exathlion. My original idea that Tirien was spawned out of was a Changing moon General that bred his own army of Beastmen Dragonbloods while his Solar Mate crafted armor and arms for them, and in so doing, got his own army of crazed zealots at his beck and call, so take that as you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T11:53:44-08:00","id":75100,"title":"","content":"@ Magnusar: Sounds neat. Once you have a solid version down, post it here for final clearance.<br /> <br /> @ Exthalion: Hmm... How about this: All Mundane crafts are rolled into one. I don't feel like there's enough overlap between the mundane craft skills and the esoteric ones to justify them all being rolled together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:52:47-08:00","id":75241,"title":"","content":"That will be wonderful, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:26:12-08:00","id":75278,"title":"","content":"what are your rules for the prodigy merit ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T16:22:29-08:00","id":75308,"title":"","content":"The prodigy merit acts as-written, plus giving a -2 exp cost reduction on charms of the appropriate ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T17:15:52-08:00","id":75329,"title":"","content":"Noodle... If all mundane crafts are being rolled into one, can I take my dot in air crafting and put it into magitech instead? I was intending to go that route later on anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","user":"CitanHyuga","date":". 02-19-2014, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T17:22:46-08:00","id":75334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CitanHyuga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/42524-recruitment-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation?p=75329#post75329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noodle... If all mundane crafts are being rolled into one, can I take my dot in air crafting and put it into magitech instead? I was intending to go that route later on anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes you can.<br /> <br /> *Curse You 10 character post minimum*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T18:46:56-08:00","id":75376,"title":"","content":"Sweet! Now I will have a 9 die minimum on all mundane type craft rolls, 11 on earth, 3 extra sux on all fire, and +2 die on all weapons XD If I craft something large that doesn't use dex... then add 2 more XD I just got SUPER boosted... lol.<br /> <br /> *Edit* And now I am almost ready to craft low end magitech artifacts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","user":"CitanHyuga","date":". 02-19-2014, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T20:23:54-08:00","id":75411,"title":"","content":"Mind if I focus on manses? They are more to my interest anyway. Oh, and you might want to rejigger your stats a little, since crafting isn't just about dice pools. There are trait minimums you have to meet. Four and five dot artifacts are only possible with max Craft, Lore, and Occult and one or two purchases of Wonder Forging Genius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T20:33:59-08:00","id":75417,"title":"","content":"I know. I have 4 occult and could have put the dot in that and easily have bought magitech with exp, but at first I decided to make it take a bit longer because that is what I originally thought would happen. Those charms were going to be two of my next three also. I wasn't thinking about crafting power 5 artifacts right away... If you are going full manse though, maybe I should. Would it be ok if I switch that dot for magitech to occult instead Noodle? I will do other things before crafting huge artifacts anyway. It will also take time to get the components.<br /> <br /> I don't mind overlap with characters so much. Even if you do craft a bit, Hyuga will find it interesting as long as you don't try to replace him. He would even enjoy a little competition from time to time. I was going to have him go a bit into manses using wyld shaping technique, but if you have that covered, perhaps I can go into Harmonious Academic Methodology instead (since I already have two lore excellencies). That way we can cover the best of both worlds quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T21:17:23-08:00","id":75431,"title":"","content":"Hey guys I managed to save a bunch of charms from the wiki before it went down and most are craft charms tell me if you are interested","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T21:46:16-08:00","id":75440,"title":"","content":"I am using normal book charms only at this point. It is all I really need. I was doing original craft rules, but with this switch I can make plenty of things. If I spend like 16 experience for the wonder-forging genius I could craft any mundane type 5-dot artifact. With that I need 3 exp to get magitech craft for 3-dot magitech artifacts. I would then need 16 more to make 5-dot magitech artifacts. I have a few useful charms and don't think I personally need them. Thank though. Exthalion might want them though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T21:52:03-08:00","id":75442,"title":"","content":"I just realized that I have started with essence 4.. guess I won't be doing that as soon as I thought XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1480-citanhyuga","name":"CitanHyuga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1480_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T13:59:23-08:00","id":75867,"title":"","content":"What do people think the following oath would rate in terms of the Oathbound flaw?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I swear by my myself, and every life I have lived and every life that will be mine, and call Heaven and its King as witness, <br /> <br /> I will not bring war upon Lookshy<br /> <br /> I will not harm its power, prestigue, or security nor aid any who seek to<br /> <br /> I will not give aid or comfort to its enemies nor support their endevors<br /> <br /> I will not seek governance over it nor permit its governance to be usurped by powers beyond its ability to resist<br /> <br /> I will ensure a place for Lookshy in this age and the next</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T14:07:37-08:00","id":75874,"title":"","content":"Hmm. [Checks Scroll of Heroes sample oaths]<br /> <br /> That's a 5pt Flaw IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T15:19:45-08:00","id":75910,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Alright so here it is Noodle my custom artifact feel free to modify it if its too or not powerful enough I have no shame in saying that I suck at balancing powers of artifact and I could not come up with something more original than raw stats modification so If you have suggestions I would be happy to read them.</span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Voltarion, The invincible sword of the sun (Level 5 Artifact)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">A relic of the primordial war Voltarion was made by the unconquered Sun himself to be gifted upon the greatest Solar swordsman. But Voltarion is not a sword contrary to its name the unconquered Sun understood that even the greatest daiklave would not be enough for his chosen, only a blade made from their very soul would be mighty enough so he created Voltarion an ornate sword hilt with it's name engraved on the guard in high holy speech and gemstones made of adamant are embedded in its handle and pommel to channel and remake the only form of weapon mighty enough for a solar to wield: the Glorious Solar Saber. Voltarion channel and augment the powers of the charm by forming a glowing double edge blade made of pure concentrated solar essence. In the high first age it was considered and honor to wield Voltarion but its powers where out matched when compared to some of the other weapons that where created during that time but in the age of sorrows its powers are enough to slay armies and topple kingdoms.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">in adition to the normal powers of the glorious solar saber Voltarion grants the following powers (Voltarion as all the stats of an orichalcum daiklave except for damage </span>that<span style=\"font-size:12px\"> is essence rating x3)</span><br /> - The weapon as the Reach tag as the blade can extend up to essence x10 yard<br /> - Adds the character essence rating in might and you are considered to have (essence) magnitude in mass combat (no extra HP).<br /> - All of the attacks made with this weapon are considered Unblockable.<br /> - <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 02-20-2014, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T16:53:15-08:00","id":75955,"title":"","content":"Might just be me, but it doesn't feel like a level five. Flat damage increase doesn't do much against Exalts combatants who usually have soak in the 20s+. The DV raise I am unsure on, as an E3 Melee 5 charm raises it permanently by 2 so it might be a little strong. Finally, the all attacks being Unblockable for free is far too cheap. Rising Sun Slash is 4m for that effect and is E4.<br /> <br /> Mostly it doesn't... feel like an E5, at least in terms of its world shaking ability. What about letting you use the old GSS formula for creating a weapon instead of being pegged to a listed artifact? Or perhaps adding the equivalent of a superior quality bonus. (Which would be reduced dot rating I think.)<br /> <br /> Again, just my two koku worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T17:50:42-08:00","id":75993,"title":"","content":"There should be a bit better now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T18:06:05-08:00","id":76000,"title":"","content":"Alright, my redesign.<br /> <br /> Voltarion, the Unconquered Soul-Blade (Artifact 4)<br /> <br /> Forged in the fires of the Daystar at the hands of the Ignis Divine, this blade was gifted to a Dawn-caste warrior prior to the Primordial war. This warrior lacked confidence, relying on mighty arms and armor rather than their own strength. The Sun took this young warrior in his arms and bestowed this blade upon them saying, &quot;No blade of metal, no wonder of artifice, can ever equal the blade that you have within your heart&quot;. And this blade proves the Sun's axiom true.<br /> <br /> When a Solar attunes to Voltation for 8 motes and uses Glorious Solar Saber, they may choose to channel the Charm through the artifact. This conjured blade uses the same traits as the normal Glorious Solar Saber, before adding the Solar's (Essence) to Accuracy, Damage and Defense. The Weapon gains the Overwhelming tag, with a minimum damage value equal to (Compassion + 1). The Solar also doubles any Overdrive motes gained through the Glorious Solar Saber.<br /> <br /> I based that off of the Perfected Kata Bracers in Oadenol's Codex. Artifact that gives a scaling benefit when a specific charm is used? Seemed pretty similar to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T19:35:22-08:00","id":76043,"title":"","content":"Those are often considered broken. The real, and huge, problem is the minimum damage there. Essence ping was one of the big contributors to the problem of lethality, and Compassion + 1 ping is going to be a lot more than essence. The biggest Overwhelming value in the game is the Grand Daiklave with 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T20:05:42-08:00","id":76061,"title":"","content":"I had a friend take a look at it and he came up with this I like the basic that Noodle took from the perfect kata bracer so he used it. Is this a bit better I wanted to keep the unblockable but you are right Exthalion it is a bit cheap but it's hard to find things that charms don't already do.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> When a Solar attunes to Voltarion for 8 motes and uses Glorious Solar Saber, they may choose to channel the Charm through the artifact. This conjured blade uses the same traits as the normal Glorious Solar Saber, before adding the Solar's (Essence) to Accuracy, Damage and Defense. The Solar also doubles any Overdrive motes gained through the Glorious Solar Saber. As a reflexive action the wielder can extend the blade up to (essence x10) yards to make attack at a distance, hit multiple opponents at the same time at different distance as a single attack or to slice through entire buildings, when used in mass combat as a solo unit this reach is transformed in (essence) Might as you cut through scores of enemies with a single swing.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 02-20-2014, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T21:21:08-08:00","id":76088,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is most of the character sheet. I am writing the backstory and filling in the intimacies right now.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_1X-SK603ZelTAMp_bwEFABN2l2IiHJsMXb9mn7qCwc/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...b9mn7qCwc/edit</a><br /> <br /> Backstory:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Yi Zhinan is a Lookshyan not born of Lookshy. The distinction has condemned him to the life of a metic, but he did not resent it overly much. Sent to the city at a young age, he proved himself worthy of admission to the Academy of Sorcery by answering a difficult koan that had troubled researchers there. Shortly after earning a brevet commission as a Sorcerer-Engineer, Yi met Karal Zhan, a Terrestrial prodigy and his commanding Chozei. He was instantly enthralled by the young Fire Aspect's passion and compassion toward the lower ranks. Through great effort Yi eventually rose to the rank of Sorcerer-Technician and traded many powerful favors to remain assigned to Zhan's command.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">For two decades, a blink of a eye in a Terrestrial's lifespan and half a lifetime to a mortal, this situation continued into the Battle of the Kumrath. What was originally a small skirmish with some of the Mask of Winter's forces near the hamlet of Kumrath turned into a major engagement when the dead troops turned out to supported by a Deathknight. It was during the battle, with Yi commanding the artillery in a desperate duel with their necromantic counterparts, that Zhan was cut off from support and surrounded. Yi violated direct orders and had his squad turn their fire to support the commander. At the same time he took up the sword of a comrade and rallied the leaderless portion of the Lookshy forces to link back up with the Zhan and drive the enemy back.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">It was in the midst of that frantic charge when Yi rejoined Zhan and finally told him how he felt. In proof that even the Most High can have terrible timing, that was when he took his second breath. There were no more words between them that day, nor between any of Yi's and any of his men. They neither fled nor attacked him. He joined the battle against the Abyssal and none questioned or hindered him. Though the battle was won, spirits were low both from the terrible casualties and from the birth of an Anathema from among their own.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">There were no words on the march home to Lookshy, and there was a great deal of space about him. The general staff was furious for his violation of orders and he was court martialed and sentenced to death. The night before his execution a familiar figure met him in prison bearing a heavy bundle. The items within were all great treasures, no doubt stolen at great personal risk, and the figure left the door open as he departed. One item, seemingly worthless besides the artifacts and chance at freedom, Yi still treasures above all the rest. It is a simply made scroll on which is written the short message. &quot;Family is more than blood.&quot;</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-21-2014, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T12:17:54-08:00","id":76481,"title":"","content":"I will put my participation on hold at the moment I don't have any good character concept in mind right now, I'll think about it and post when I have something.<br /> <br /> Nice character concept Exthalion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/208